tyle="min-height:1.5em">You will support the full lifecycle of aerospace hardware, from manufacturability assessment and process development through qualification, certification, and production readiness. Working closely with Design Engineering, Materials &amp; Processes, Quality, Testing, and Manufacturing teams, you will contribute to the delivery of flight-ready components across TEC's propulsion and space systems programs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a technically demanding role with direct impact on flight hardware development, manufacturing capability, and future production scalability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the manufacturing and qualification of mission-critical flight hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop, optimize, and qualify LPBF processes for a range of high-performance alloys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and manage material characterization campaigns, support test execution, and analyze the resulting data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take over build preparation, LPBF process simulation, and process monitoring data analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute qualification and certification activities for AM hardware in accordance with aerospace requirements and internal quality processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot manufacturing challenges and drive continuous improvement in process capability, quality, productivity, and inspection methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Author technical documentation and collaborate with internal teams, external suppliers, laboratories, and certification bodies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Aerospace Engineering, or related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with metal LPBF systems in an industrial environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in LPBF process development, material and part verification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge in material characterization methodologies, including the selection and interpretation of material property and mechanical testing data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in CAD for part design modification, LPBF build design, and support generation. Experience with Siemens NX and PLM tools such as Teamcenter is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication, analytical problem-solving, and effective collaboration across multidisciplinary and international teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in LPBF process and hardware qualification for complex aerospace propulsion systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of DFAM principles, LPBF process physics and parameters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with aerospace materials such as nickel-based superalloys, titanium alloys, copper alloys, as well as stainless steels. Refractory alloys is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience in machine operation, material characterization, including metallography, microstructural characterization, and mechanical testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in additive manufacturing process simulation solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Explo