oration-company/mait-additive-manufacturing-engineer-dusseldorf-239673","tags":["MAIT"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Düsseldorf","created_at":1792312821},{"slug":"gnc-engineer-munich-325147","company_name":"The Exploration Company","title":"GNC Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Here at The Exploration Company, we are building spacecrafts for humanity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want you as a talented GNC Engineer to contribute to the GNC subsystem design, testing, verification and validation of our vehicles. As a GNC Engineer, you must have a firm grasp of spacecraft GNC concepts and applications. You will work on all aspects of the GNC life cycle: spacecraft and mission conceptual design, subsystem requirements development, algorithm development, software implementation and testing, operations, and post-flight analysis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your capacity as a GNC Engineer, your role will be continuously evolving, but day to day your duties will include to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in the design and implementation of the AOCS/GNC subsystem of The Exploration Company’ spacecraft for a wide variety of spacecraft and space missions to include LEO operations, Reentry, and Rendezvous and Docking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, synthesis, test, implementation, verification, and validation of GNC algorithms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement the GNC code into the Flight Software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop high fidelity 6 degrees of freedom models and simulations to analyze the system performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform design, optimization, and dispersion analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform multi-disciplinary spacecraft systems trades and investigations to improve The Exploration Company’ spacecraft performance and reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AOCS/GNC hardware specification, selection, modeling and simulation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop software automation tools for GNC design, analysis, testing and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate and verify your GNC software via algorithm unit testing, Monte Carlo analysis, and software-in-the-loop and hardware-in-the-loop testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting of test results and analysis, with a focus on efficiency and automation of documentation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we would love to see from you</strong>:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In the role of GNC Engineer ideally, you will have the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc. in Aerospace or related engineering discipline. A higher degree is considered advantageous.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of classical dynamics, orbital and flight mechanics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of control and estimation techniques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with flight physics simulation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software development experience in C++, Python and MATLAB/Simulink.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for advancing the commercial space industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly motivated to work in a fast paced, autonomously driven, and demanding start-up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English. German or French is an asset.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immediate consideration and we will be in touch shortly. <br /> <br /><em>The Exploration Company is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status or disability status. Relocation assistance is provided for those willing to relocate including visa sponsorship where applicable.  </em><br /><br /><em><br />All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check, which will be subject to the country, role, and project you applied for. By submitting your application, you acknowledge and agree that any offer of employment may be conditional upon successful condition of this check. The Exploration Company partners with Zinc Work Limited located in the UK (Zinc), a third-party provider, to ensure this process as efficient and transparent as possible. <br /><br />If applicable, you will receive an email from Zinc upon acceptance of your offer with a link to a secure portal where you can provide the required information to Zinc. </em><br /></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/the-exploration-company/gnc-engineer-munich-325147","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich, Germany","created_at":1792312821},{"slug":"remote-manager-director-partnerships-dach-201614","company_name":"Roompricegenie","title":"Remote Manager (Director) Partnerships DACH (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About RoomPriceGenie</strong> ✨🧞‍♂️</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2017, RoomPriceGenie is dedicated to helping hoteliers around the globe achieve optimal pricing. 🌍 We understand that many small hotels face challenges with digitalization, making their operations increasingly complex and often resulting in lost revenue. This is where we come in!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have developed a powerful solution that enables hotels to set the right prices in just seconds. ⏱️ Our state-of-the-art algorithm analyzes both internal hotel data and market trends to recommend pricing strategies that enhance revenue and improve booking rates. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With customers spanning the globe—from the USA and Canada to Iceland, South Africa, China, Slovenia, Italy, and the UK—RoomPriceGenie has made a meaningful impact in the hospitality industry, and our clients love the results. ❤️</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we are excited to expand our customer base and spread the word about how we can support hoteliers in optimizing their pricing strategies. We invite you to join us on this journey! We actively encourage applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds to enrich our team and drive innovation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The goal of this role is pipeline revenue, driven through relationships. The Partner BDM is where the global partnership strategy meets the market, and you own the partner pipeline and revenue target for your region — you are the person who drives the strategy to meet and exceed that number. Every relationship, every lead, every partner conversation in your territory goes through you. You execute all three partnership pillars locally — integration depth, reseller acquisition, and long tail activation — and you feed the national programs run by Isabel and the Director of Reseller Partnerships with the contacts, intelligence, and HubSpot discipline that makes those programs possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role also carries a global partner management component. In addition to your regional territory, you will be assigned one or two global partner accounts — relationships that span multiple BDM regions and require a consistent strategic, commercial presence above the regional level. You will manage these accounts directly, briefing with the Global Partner Marketing Manager before any senior contact touchpoint and feeding back the account intelligence that informs RPG's global partner strategy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The BDM is not a lone hunter. You are supported by intelligence briefs from the Director of Partnership Strategy, onboarding infrastructure from the Partner Operation and Enablement Manager, co-sell support from the Director of Channel Growth Reseller, and global account context from the Global Partner Marketing Manager. The discipline of using those inputs — requesting briefs before first calls, completing HubSpot fields that trigger Isabel's onboarding, registering every lead in Introw on the day — is what makes the whole system work.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>Your Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline and revenue ownership — your region</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the partner pipeline and revenue target for your region — you are the person who drives the strategy to meet and exceed this number, not just a contributor to it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a consistent bottoms-up pipeline plan, built up against your region's targets and TAM — showing exactly how your book of business adds up to your target, by partner type and by deal stage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forecast monthly, ahead of the full-team KPR review — reforecasting pipeline and revenue coverage against target, reconciling to the latest refreshed regional targets/TAM where these have moved, so gaps are visible early and plans can be adjusted before target dates, not after</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regional partner development — all partner types</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and manage the full partner portfolio in your territory: integration partners, resellers, consultants, hotel management companies, and referral partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source new reseller and consultant contacts in your region — using the Ideal Reseller Partner Profile as the qualification standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute the partner conversation playbook for each contact type: open with the partner intelligence brief, use the CS manager and KAM conversation guides for integration partners, apply the reseller screening framework for agency contacts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Request a partner intelligence brief from the Director Channel Growth - Integration before every first partner outreach — no first conversation without a brief</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete the 4 mandatory HubSpot fields (deal stage, partner fields, agreement file, partnership type) before advancing any deal past the signed stage — this triggers Isabel's onboarding program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Register every qualified lead in Introw on the day it is received, tagged by source type (integration referral / reseller / consultant / reactivated dormant)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Global Partner Account Management</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own one or two assigned global partner accounts — relationships where the partner operates across multiple BDM territories and requires consistent commercial management above the regional level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the regional strategy for each assigned global account that generates pipeline — not just relationship maintenance; you are responsible for identifying where the pipeline comes from in your territory and driving it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with Global Partner Marketing Manager before any senior touchpoint at a global partner account — global commercial context will be provided; you provide the regional relationship intelligence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the account relationship at the appropriate contact levels (sales, CS, KAM, implementation) — applying the multi-level engagement model from the Partner Activation Playbook</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed the Head of Global Partnerships and the Global Partner Marketing Manager with global account intelligence after every significant touchpoint — health signals, competitive intelligence, co-marketing opportunities, and any escalation requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the coordination of co-marketing and QBR activity with the global partner where it involves your region</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Long Tail Activation — Regional subset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own your regional subset of the 272 dormant signed partners — the Director Channel Growth - Reseller &amp; Consultant,provides the segmented list, you own the outreach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute the tiered re-engagement approach: Tier 1 (60–90 days dormant) with a personalized message within the first week of assignment; Tier 2 with re-qualification before any effort; Tier 3 with a single attempt then escalation to Isabel to archive</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report progress on your regional dormant subset to Isabel weekly during the H2 activation sprint</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market intelligence and HubSpot discipline</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Surface partner contacts and market intelligence to the Reseller PM in the bi-weekly regional intel exchange — which reseller types are gaining traction, which are declining, what competitive signals are emerging</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag any integration partner conversation where an all-in-one competitive angle appears — the Strategy Manager updates the competitive library with field intelligence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain HubSpot contact and deal records at the expected quality standard — the data in HubSpot is what the whole team uses to run the business; poor data quality breaks Isabel's onboarding, Isabel's dormancy tracking, and Introw attribution simultaneously</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in the monthly full-team KPR review — presenting your regional lead pipeline and flagging any structural blockers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in a B2B business development, partnerships, or commercial account management role — ideally in SaaS, hospitality technology, or a related field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrates advanced proficiency in German (C2 level), with excellent command of both</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of building relationships and generating pipeline from scratch in a defined territory — not managing inbound, but generating outbound</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating across multiple partner types and conversation styles in a single week — integration partnership conversations require a different approach than reseller qualification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">HubSpot or CRM discipline — this is a non-negotiable requirement; the quality of your data determines the quality of the team's output</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in the target territory — regional credibility and proximity to local partners is part of the role</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing network in the hotel technology ecosystem (PMS, channel manager, consultants, or revenue management) in the relevant territory</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing global or multi-territory accounts in addition to a local territory portfolio</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Introw, PartnerStack, Reditus, or similar partner and commission tracking platforms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Revenue management or hospitality operations background — understanding how an independent hotel owner thinks is a genuine advantage in partner conversations</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer at RoomPriceGenie</strong> 💪</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At RoomPriceGenie, we don’t just offer jobs; we offer an adventure! 🚀 Join us in an exciting startup atmosphere where you can grow your career while changing the world for tens of thousands of independent hoteliers. 🌍 Our global and diverse team is fueled by passion and a shared mission. We thrive in a culture that’s all about transparency, respect, and making a real impact together. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what you can expect when you become part of our Genie family:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-First Model</strong>: Work from (almost!) anywhere. 🌍🧑‍💻 Some roles need you in a specific country or time zone — we'll always flag that in the job ad. And whenever you like, come co-work with us in Mannheim, Berlin, or Sydney. 🏢</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>One Team, One Vision, One Goal:</strong> We’re in this together! 🤝 Our Genies are laser-focused on our mission, collaborating to make magic happen. ✨ It’s no wonder we score a stellar 9.3 from our team members! 🌟</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Epic Team Gatherings:</strong> Every year, we bring our global crew together 🌎 for a week of networking, brainstorming, and fun. 🎉 Plus, enjoy regular hangouts in our offices to keep the camaraderie alive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth and Development:</strong> We’re all about lifelong learning! 📚 Level up your skills with personal and professional development opportunities. You’ll even snag up to three extra days off each year to focus on your growth. 📈</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5 Years? 5 Weeks!</strong> Stick with us, and we’ll reward your loyalty. After five years, you’ll earn an incredible five weeks of bonus vacation time 🏖️ to recharge and explore the world. 🌍</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Birthday Celebrations:</strong> It’s your day, so take it off! 🎂 Celebrate your birthday the way you want, guilt-free.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible Hours:</strong> We get it—life happens! ⏰ We offer flexible working hours to help you balance your work and personal life seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellbeing Matters:</strong> Your mental health is a top priority. 🧘 Every Genie gets access to Headspace, the leading meditation app, to help you cultivate a happier, healthier, and more zen life. 🌿</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>BetterHelp Support: </strong>We also offer <strong>BetterHelp</strong>, a professional online therapy and counseling platform, giving you additional support whenever you need it.<strong>💛🧠</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We kindly ask that recruitment agencies refrain from reaching out regarding this vacancy. Thank you for your understanding.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/roompricegenie/remote-manager-director-partnerships-dach-201614","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote Germany","created_at":1792312821},{"slug":"remote-head-of-ux-75548","company_name":"Roompricegenie","title":"Remote Head of UX (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About RoomPriceGenie</strong> ✨🧞‍♂️</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2017, RoomPriceGenie is dedicated to helping hoteliers around the globe achieve optimal pricing. 🌍 We understand that many small hotels face challenges with digitalization, making their operations increasingly complex and often resulting in lost revenue. This is where we come in!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have developed a powerful solution that enables hotels to set the right prices in just seconds. ⏱️ Our state-of-the-art algorithm analyzes both internal hotel data and market trends to recommend pricing strategies that enhance revenue and improve booking rates. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With customers spanning the globe—from the USA and Canada to Iceland, South Africa, China, Slovenia, Italy, and the UK—RoomPriceGenie has made a meaningful impact in the hospitality industry, and our clients love the results. ❤️</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we are excited to expand our customer base and spread the word about how we can support hoteliers in optimizing their pricing strategies. We invite you to join us on this journey! We actively encourage applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds to enrich our team and drive innovation. </p><h1></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Head of UX at RoomPriceGenie, you'll lead our small but mighty design and research team of two product designers and one user researcher.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't an IC role where you'll be pushing pixels or running sessions yourself. It's a leadership role focused on building the function, championing the team, and setting them up for success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll set the strategic direction for how design and research operates, advocate for the team at leadership level, and create the conditions for your people to do their best work. You'll also play a key role in raising design and research maturity across the wider product organisation — guiding better decisions through clearer systems, guidelines, and shared insight.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h2>Leadership Representation &amp; Advocacy</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion design and research as a strategic partner that shapes the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Leadership to translate strategic business priorities into a clear, sequenced roadmap for Design &amp; Research.</p></li></ul><h2>Strategic Direction &amp; Vision</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set a clear vision for the design and research function — defining what success looks like, where it's heading, and how it contributes to the company's overall strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise design and research maturity by providing constructive critique and quality oversight to support high-quality product outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create the space for the team to work on foundational initiatives that scale team impact. For example: evolving the component library into a robust design system and establishing clear design and content playbooks to drive consistency, efficiency, and quality.</p></li></ul><h2>AI Operations &amp; Enablement</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the strategic direction for how AI fits into the design &amp; research workflow — where it accelerates, where craft stays human, and set clear guardrails for how the wider org uses it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a culture where the team integrates AI into product work — evolving their craft and building fluency through practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure designers and researchers play a key role in shaping product and AI direction, grounding decisions in user insight and design perspective.</p></li></ul><h2>Stakeholder Collaboration</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for Design Thinking to be embedded throughout the product life cycle, shaping ideas and guiding decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively identify large, strategic UX opportunities that span across the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Navigate competing priorities between leadership direction and team capacity, ensuring the team stays focused on high-impact work.</p></li></ul><h2>Team Development &amp; Coaching</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide ongoing coaching, mentoring, and constructive feedback through regular one-to-ones — focused on the development and growth of your team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build clear career frameworks and progression paths for Design and Research.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Encourage continuous learning, adaptability, and development within the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine understanding of both design and research disciplines, even if your background leans more toward one. You don't need to be an expert in both, but you need to value and support both equally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in a senior design leadership role is required — you've owned a function, led teams of designers and researchers, and have a track record of influencing product direction at the leadership level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of advocating for both disciplines at the leadership level and influencing product strategy, not just delivering on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or maturing a design function: establishing processes, systems, playbooks, or ways of working from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about AI and how it's changing the way design and research teams work — you don't need to be an expert, but you should be excited about figuring this out with the team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Soft Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A compassionate, proactive leadership style that creates emotional safety for the people around you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident navigating difficult stakeholder dynamics without losing your composure or your team's trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator who can translate design value into language that resonates with leadership, product, and engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable giving and receiving direct feedback — you see it as a gift.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in or familiarity with the hotel or travel industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with building or scaling teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining a design system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in scale-ups or startups — you're comfortable with ambiguity and thrive in environments that are still finding their shape.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer at RoomPriceGenie</strong> 💪</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At RoomPriceGenie, we don’t just offer jobs; we offer an adventu