You will be responsible for the successful implementation of customer projects in the field of Converged Security - from order receipt through to successful commissioning.</p></li><li><p>In this role, you will coordinate the various project stakeholders and ensure smooth collaboration between customers, subcontractors, technicians, and colleagues from Presales Consulting.</p></li><li><p>You will plan and manage budgets, deadlines, resources, and project progress, while keeping customer requirements in mind at all times.</p></li><li><p>Together with the customer, you will analyze technical and organizational requirements and oversee their implementation in hardware and software solutions.</p></li><li><p>You will ensure that business processes and security requirements are optimally mapped in our systems and applications.</p></li><li><p>You coordinate hardware installation by external service providers and plan the subsequent testing, commissioning, and acceptance of the systems by our service technicians.</p></li><li><p>For software-related services, you work closely with our specialists from Presales Consulting and support resource and deployment planning.</p></li><li><p>You identify project risks early on, develop appropriate solutions, and ensure the financially successful execution of your projects.</p></li><li><p>In addition, you organize project meetings, training sessions, and customer acceptance tests, and serve as the primary point of contact throughout the entire project.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3><strong>Key Qualifications</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Completed technical training, e.g., as an IT systems technician (m/f/d), electronics technician (m/f/d), IT specialist (m/f/d), or a bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, information technology, security engineering, industrial engineering, or a comparable field.</p></li><li><p>Initial experience in managing technical projects, ideally in the fields of security engineering, IT systems, access control, time and attendance management, or building automation.</p></li><li><p>Technical understanding of both hardware and software solutions.</p></li><li><p>Enthusiasm for integrating technical systems with business processes and translating customer requirements into practical solutions.</p></li><li><p>A structured, independent, and cost-effective approach to work.</p></li><li><p>Experience coordinating various stakeholders, service providers, or project partners is a plus.</p></li><li><p>Strong communication and organizational skills.</p></li><li><p>Very good command of German and good written and spoken English.</p></li><li><p>Class B driver’s license.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Your Benefits</strong></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What makes working with us great?</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;">We take care of you while you take care of your business! We listen better and take a closer look. Our aim is to build long-term relationships based on mutual respect and trust.<br><br>That's why we offer you:</p><ul><li><p><strong>A modern work environment:</strong> Working from home as your primary workplace, flexible flex-time arrangements for an optimal work-life balance, and the opportunity to work independently with a high degree of autonomy.</p></li><li><p><strong>Every minute counts:</strong> With us, your travel time to client visits is paid as working time.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company car:</strong> A neutral company car available for personal use as well, complete with a fuel card valid throughout Europe.</p></li><li><p><strong>Strong team:</strong> Collaborative work and open communication with experienced colleagues from sales, service, and technical teams.</p></li><li><p><strong>Impact</strong>: Play a crucial role in the successful completion of converged security and workforce management projects that simultaneously ensure the highest security standards and a smooth daily experience 