tomers, but equally passionate about developing our people with new skills and ways of working.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Your Role at ITQ:</h3><p>As a Cloud Consultant/Architect, you will support our clients in transforming their traditional data centers into modern, flexible, and efficient software-defined environments. Working closely with customers, you’ll understand their business requirements and develop tailored solutions using the latest technologies. You’ll be there to save the day—by simplifying complex data center infrastructures or cloud environments, reducing costs, and increasing overall performance.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>The Benefits at ITQ:</h3><p><strong>Integration:</strong></p><ul><li><p>A comprehensive onboarding process, followed by an informal lunch or dinner with your “buddy.”<br></p></li></ul><p><strong>ITQ:</strong></p><ul><li><p>A friendly atmosphere with a strong corporate culture.</p></li><li><p>Regular team events (team building, after-work events, partner/publisher conferences).</p></li><li><p>Flexible working hours and the option for remote work.<br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Excellence:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Collaboration with top experts in their field, participation in regular trade fairs and events, as well as global networking opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Involvement in innovative and large-scale projects.</p></li><li><p>Continuous training programs and sponsored certifications.</p></li><li><p>A clear and ambitious vision for the future, with openness to your ideas and feedback.<br></p></li></ul><h3>What We Offer You:</h3><ul><li><p>Numerous opportunities for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p>A competitive salary package, a collective bonus, and an annual budget for training and certifications.</p></li><li><p>A company car or mobility budget.</p></li><li><p>A remote work budget to set up your workspace.</p></li><li><p>Social benefits such as retirement provisions and an employee savings plan.</p></li><li><p>The chance to be part of a warm and inclusive team—the ITQ family.<br></p></li></ul><h3>Your Tasks and Technologies:</h3><p>You bring solid experience in one or more of the following areas:</p><ul><li><p>VMware technologies (one or more) such as VMware vSphere, vSAN, Aria Operations, or NSX; experience in a Dell VxRail environment is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p>Design, implementation, and optimization of AWS architectures, including cloud migrations, security, and cost optimization.</p></li><li><p>Planning, implementation, and administration of Red Hat Enterprise Linux, as well as related technologies such as OpenShift, Ansible, and Satellite.</p></li><li><p>HashiCorp technologies, particularly Terraform for Infrastructure-as-Code and Vault for secret management.</p></li></ul><p>You are hands-on experienced with Hyper-Converged Infrastructure (HCI) solutions—experience in this area is an advantage.<br>You have architectural knowledge in the field of SDDC with a solid understanding of x86 virtualization, operating systems, advanced networking, and storage architectures.<br>You hold up-to-date industry-standard certifications and are willing to acquire further certifications.</p><p><br></p> <br> <h3>What We Expect From You:</h3><ul><li><p>You are passionate about your work as a Consultant or Architect and can identify customer use cases and translate them into concrete solutions.</p></li><li><p>You are fluent in German and can communicate confidently in English.</p></li><li><p>You are curious about new technologies—because that’s exactly your thing.</p></li><li><p>You live in Germany.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/itq/remote-cloud-consultant-architect-dusseldorf-261020","tags":["DE - SDDC","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792312288},{"slug":"senior-industrialisation-engineer-munich-283776","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior Industrialisation Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure style="text-align:center;"><a target="_blank" href="https://www.eftmobility.com/en/company/"><img style="width:800px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/f4l5lyenf6/EFT_Mobility.jpg"></a></figure><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Join EFT Mobility at a pivotal time as we revolutionize the future of electric transport, focusing on cutting-edge Electric Powertrain (EFT) solutions for high-reliability applications, including UAV power systems. We are a fast-growing, dynamic company where every engineer plays a direct, hands-on role in bringing our innovative, safety-critical products to life. If you thrive on ensuring product quality and solving complex, real-world problems, we want you on our team.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>We are seeking a highly skilled, execution-driven and hands-on <strong>Senior Industrialisation Engineer</strong> to bridge the gap between R&amp;D and mass manufacturing for our battery packs and charger product lines.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>In this role, your primary focus will be the <strong>electro-mechanical process s</strong>teps and optimizations required to transform a functional prototype into a robust, high-yield, and highly scalable series product. You will take ownership of the product lifecycle immediately following the initial prototype build phase. Collaborating closely with our external Contract Manufacturers (CMs), you will co-architect the manufacturing lines, advise on critical assembly fixtures, and pave the way for a production ramp-up from pre-series batches into stable mass production.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Review designs</strong> directly following R&amp;D prototype runs to actively catch and eliminate mechanical tolerance stack-ups and assembly risks before tooling begins.</p></li><li><p> <strong>Optimise</strong> the design, sourcing, and validation of <strong>mechanical assembly jigs</strong>, cell-alignment fixtures, glueing fixtures, laser-welding beds to optimize line repeatability and operator safety. </p></li><li><p>Collaborate regularly with <strong>Contract Manufacturers to optimise and release assembly line setup</strong>s, resolve technical build bottlenecks, and transition pilot runs into high-yield mass production. </p></li><li><p> <strong>Conduct hands-on Design of Experiments</strong> in the lab and factory floor to establish locked-in process windows for automated gluing, thermal interface material (TIM) dispensing, and torque specs. </p></li><li><p><strong>Co-Own build failures</strong> together with the contract manufacturer to rapidly drive engineering adjustments and optimize first-pass yields. Page: 1/3 </p></li><li><p> Oversee the <strong>EoL failures</strong>, analyse them and implement solutions to improve yield.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h4><ul><li><p> Experience: 8+ years of experience as an Industrialization, Manufacturing, or NPI (New Product Introduction) Engineer, specifically driving the scale-up (upto 10-30k units) of battery modules/packs, power electronics enclosures, or high-reliability electromechanical systems.</p></li><li><p>Technical Skills: Highly skilled in (mechanical) production processes, experience with failure analysis and production methods in a semi-automised production environment.</p></li><li><p> Hands-on Workshop Mentality: A deeply practical engineer who thrives on the shop floor or in the prototype lab. You have no hesitation when it comes to standing at the line, personally assembling a battery module to understand a build bottleneck, or physically tearing down hardware to isolate a defect.</p></li><li><p> Design Review &amp; CAD Interpretation: Strong ability to navigate, interpret, and evaluate 3D CAD models and engineering drawings.</p></li><li><p>Communication: Strong ability to translate technical failure data intoactionable engineering changes.</p></li><li><p> Project Management &amp; CM Governance: Strong capability to coordinate complex technical tasks across internal engineering design teams and external contract manufacturers, with the technical confidence to regularly audit and challenge the work of the CM's internal industrialization teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>Your Benefits:&nbsp;</strong></h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Direct impact: </strong>See your contributions rapidly integrated from cutting-edge research into industrialized products, flying in the field within short development cycles.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Culture &amp; Environment: </strong>A dynamic, fast-paced, and collaborative startup environment with flat hierarchies, efficient collaboration, and a strong emphasis on continuous learning opportunities.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Work-life Balance: </strong>We offer flexible work schedules, and 30 days of paid vacation each year to support your personal and professional life.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Lunch Benefit: </strong>We promote healthy eating and the well-being of our employees with a monthly lunch budget.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Mobility Benefit: </strong>With our mobility budget, we pay your “Germany Ticket” for work or personal use monthly.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> We support your physical well-being with a company-subsidized eGym Wellpass membership, giving you access to thousands of gyms and sports facilities.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Language Courses: </strong>German isn’t your mother tongue? We sponsor German courses for you to quickly learn and integrate even more.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8">&nbsp;</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/quantum-systems-gmbh/senior-industrialisation-engineer-munich-283776","tags":["Hardware"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Munich, Bayern, Germany","created_at":1792312287},{"slug":"senior-data-analyst-gilching-96906","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"(Senior) Data Analyst (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;">As a Data Analyst (m/f/d) focussing in the land domain for unmanned ground vehicles, you will play a leading role within the Cloud &amp; Data Team, owning the evaluation, interpretation, and continuous improvement of analytics for large-scale telemetry and system data. You will shape how data is analyzed across products and platforms, enabling data-driven decisions in R&amp;D, production, testing, and customer support. You will work with a highly skilled team and collaborate closely with stakeholders across the globe. In this role, you will combine advanced analytical skills, algorithm development, and technical leadership to build robust, automated evaluation methods for complex technical systems.<br><br></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Lead tool-based analysis of telemetry and system data across R&amp;D, production, testing, and customer support</p></li><li><p>Own and evolve the data analysis toolchain, ensuring scalability, reliability, and reproducibility</p></li><li><p>Design, implement, and maintain automated data evaluation and testing pipelines</p></li><li><p>Drive the design and use of database solutions for large-scale telemetry data</p></li><li><p>Evaluate, prototype, and deploy advanced analytics and AI-based methods, including anomaly detection, predictive maintenance, and online monitoring of subsystems</p></li><li><p>Collaborate closely with Data Engineers and Cloud Engineers to integrate analytics into production systems</p></li><li><p>Communicate insights and analytical results clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p>Act as a technical mentor and analytical authority within the team</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong><br></strong></h4><h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong><br></h4><p><strong>Data Analysis &amp; Algorithms</strong></p><ul><li><p>Strong hands-on experience using python for data analysis and algorithm development</p></li><li><p>Solid understanding of statistics, hypothesis testing, and data validation techniques</p></li><li><p>Experience designing custom evaluation algorithms for complex or high-frequency data</p></li><li><p>Strong experience with time-series analysis and telemetry data</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Data &amp; Databases</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience working with timeseries, structured, unstructured and analytical databases</p></li><li><p>Good understanding of efficient data storage, retrieval, and optimization strategies</p></li><li><p>Experience collaborating on data models and analytical interfaces</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Advanced Analytics</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience evaluating or implementing machine learning or AI-based methods (e.g. anomaly detection, predictive maintenance, trend analysis)</p></li><li><p>Understanding of model validation, robustness, and monitoring in production contexts</p></li></ul><p><br></p><h4><strong>Why Quantum-Systems:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>We believe in the power of combined&nbsp;efforts: straightforward tech expertise&nbsp;paired with a customer-centric focus.</p></li><li><p>We are industry pioneers&nbsp;who are ambitious, bold,&nbsp;and visionary. </p></li><li><p>We push limits, think&nbsp;outside-the-box and strive&nbsp;for technological excellence to&nbsp;shape the future of aerial data.</p></li><li><p>We promise to be your runway&nbsp;for individual and professional&nbsp;growth.</p></li></ul><p><strong><br></strong></p><h4><strong>Our benefits:</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Company pension scheme: </strong>We support you so that you can already make provisions for later.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible working hours: </strong>With trust-based working hours, you are not only responsible for your working hours, but also for your work-life balance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile Work:</strong> If things get a little busy in the office, you have the option to work remotely one flexible day per week to create the right balance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stay active:</strong> With EGYM Wellpass, you get access to thousands of fitness and sports facilities — and of course, we subsidize the membership.</p></li><li><p><strong>Bike-Leasing: </strong>We support you in staying environmentally mobile and healthy.</p></li><li><p><strong>Corporate Benefits: </strong>Your opportunity for attractive offers and discounts from well-known suppliers and brands, e.g. Adidas, Apple, Expedia.</p></li><li><p><strong>Employee events: </strong>We not only want to grow together, but also celebrate our successes together.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lunch-Card: </strong>Be powerful with delicious energy, daily lunch budget is sponsored.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company Shut