&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Your personal information will be processed in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://bw-ess.com/bw-ess-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bwessmanagementgmbh/senior-treasury-manager-uk-london-295883","tags":["FP&A and Treasury"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792324522},{"slug":"forward-deployed-consultant-london-254063","company_name":"Monday.com","title":"Forward Deployed Consultant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> is the AI work platform powering the most ambitious teams. 250,000+ customers across departments use us to bring people, workflows, and AI agents together on one flexible platform where AI doesn't just assist, it executes. We move fast, build things that matter, and foster an ownership-driven culture where you're empowered to shape how organisations work and outpace their competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team is growing and we are looking for a Forward Deployed Consultant to join our Professional Services team! In this role, you will train, advise and consult, and build with customers to optimize their use of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> AI work platform during the course of an AI transformation, implementation, or ongoing managed services engagement. You will design and build the AI-native solutions that get them there, from intelligent workflows and agents to the automations and reporting their business relies on. You will run engagements both independently and as a part of a delivery team collaborating with deployment strategists and engineers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note that this is a hybrid position with three days/week in our <strong>London</strong> office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the Role</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead AI transformation and implementation engagements for <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> customers, designing and building tailored solutions using agents, vibe-coded applications, and other advanced capabilities of the monday AI work platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with client stakeholders, running the discovery that uncovers their desired business outcomes, and ensure successful adoption of the solutions you deliver across their organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consult on business process design, mapping how work moves through a customer's organization and recommending the process changes that should be made before the solution is built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design sophisticated workflows and relational data structures within the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> platform to solve complex business cases, partnering with technical resources for data conversions, integrations, and agentic engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively leverage monday AI and external Generative/Agentic AI tools to accelerate solution design, automate complex business logic, and deliver intelligent workflows for our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the project manager on standalone engagements, building and executing on project plans that ensure deliverables stay on-time and on-budget, and delivering defined scope alongside a deployment strategist on larger ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run online webinars, training sessions, consultations, and one-on-one demos that show customers how our product capabilities translate into business value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce the documentation, walkthroughs, and exit artifacts for your engagements that allow customers to operate, maintain, and extend what you built independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the voice of the customer by advocating for their needs and influencing the product development roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute the patterns and reusable assets you develop in the field back to our shared asset library.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Requirements</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience as a forward-deployed consultant, implementation consultant, solutions consultant, or technical project manager in enterprise software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading software implementation or managed services projects that required hands-on build and system configuration in project management, CRM, service desk, or collaborative work management software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in Generative and Agentic AI tools, with a strong understanding of how to leverage AI in streamlining work productivity and building intelligent workflows and agents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with what keeps AI reliable in production, including human review, checking outputs, and knowing when a deterministic automation is the better answer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem solving skills, rooted in computational thinking, systems design, and an understanding of relational data structures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business process design and consulting experience, with the business acumen to frame an engagement around customer outcomes, and the judgment to read the implicit problem behind an explicit request.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of integration platforms (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://make.com">make.com</a>, Zapier) sufficient to configure lightweight integrations yourself, with foundational knowledge of APIs (GraphQL) and MCP a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong customer-facing and presentation skills with the ability to establish credibility with client stakeholders and executives, and to clearly articulate technical topics to a non-technical audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to rapidly learn and take advantage of new concepts, business models, and technologies across a changing set of customers and industries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detail-oriented with strong project management skills, comfortable running engagements independently and working across several at once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Superb written and verbal communication skills, with a positive attitude, empathy, high energy, and the ability to take initiative and adapt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel up to 20% of the time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BA or BS degree preferred.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Please note that this role is hybrid.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visa sponsorship for this role is currently not available.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We hire talented individuals, regardless of gender, race, ethnicity, ancestry, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, military or veteran status, cultural background, religious beliefs, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mondaycom/forward-deployed-consultant-london-254063","tags":["Delivery & Solutions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792323617},{"slug":"professional-services-team-manager-forward-deployed-consulting-london-479453","company_name":"Monday.com","title":"Professional Services Team Manager - Forward Deployed Consulting","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com"><strong>monday.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> is the AI work platform powering the most ambitious teams. 250,000+ customers across departments use us to bring people, workflows, and AI agents together on one flexible platform where AI doesn't just assist, it executes. We move fast, build things that matter, and foster an ownership-driven culture where you're empowered to shape how organisations work and outpace their competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the group / About the team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>'s team is growing and we are looking for a Professional Services Team Manager to join our team in London! In this role, you will lead and grow a team of Forward Deployed Consultants responsible for implementing the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>'s AI Work platform for our customers. Your team is responsible for advising and consulting with customers to build and optimise solutions using <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> products. We’re looking for a results-oriented team leader with a demonstrated track record of successful customer outcomes.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure the high-quality, on-time delivery of high volumes of projects of varying length and complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise and enable the team on the different components of a project lifecycle, including discovery, requirements, configuration, testing, execution, roll-out, training, and launch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with cross-functional stakeholders, including Customer Success, Sales, and Partners, to drive efficient and reliable project delivery for our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a coach, mentor, and leader to individuals on the team, while setting expectations on performance based on data, using consistent feedback and transparency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and execute process improvements, policy development, delivery methods, metrics, and tools in support of client delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the strategy to onboard, enable, and expand usage and revenue with customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accountability for team operations and the KPIs used to measure the team’s success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruit, hire and train new team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build programs and initiatives to drive continuous internal process improvement and enable the teams' ability to scale</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5-10 years experience in Implementation, Professional Services, or Managed Services, preferably in SaaS or at technology consulting firms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3-5+ years of people management experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience with project management, CRM, service desk, and/or collaborative work management software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience delivering or overseeing AI-related implementations - including AI workflow automation, AI-powered platform features, or AI transformation projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with AI tools and the ability to advise customers on how to incorporate AI capabilities into their workflows and solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to successfully navigate complex organisational structures (internal and external)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable transforming department strategy into tactical initiatives and executing on them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process-focused and metrics-driven (desire to instil a process that can scale)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience estimating delivery effort and creating Statements of Work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly effective communication and interpersonal skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An amazing team player who can collaborate with multiple internal and external stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mondaycom/professional-services-team-manager-forward-deployed-consulting-london-479453","tags":["Delivery & Solutions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792323617},{"slug":"lead-mechanical-sector-nuclear-m-f-bridgwater-405192","company_name":"T.E.S","title":"Lead Mechanical sector nuclear (m/f)","description":"<p><strong>Technical Engineering Support</strong> (<strong>TES</strong>) is an <strong>engineering</strong> company created over 30 years ago, specializing in the <strong>coordination</strong> of <strong>tests</strong> and industrial <strong>commissioning</strong>. TES also supports its customers in participating in <strong>studies</strong> and coordinating the <strong>assembly</strong> of industrial equipment.</p><p>As part of our activity, we have a position to fill as <strong>Lead Mechanical</strong> for <strong>nuclear project Hinkley-Point</strong> <strong>UK</strong>.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Completions orientated Site Wide Records Discipline Lead interfacing with MEH (Mechanical, Electricity, HVAC) Area LTQR* Coordinators &amp; Technicians, MDT and relevant stakeholders to capture &amp; process discipline specific LTQR deliverables on time and in line with project deadlines ensuring completion and delivery of associated scope LTQR deliverables to support End of Erection Status Reports.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Accountabilities :</p><ol><li><p>Single POC for Discipline specific records</p></li><li><p>Technical expert liaison with MEH Site and Assurance Leads</p></li><li><p>Interface with MEH completions team re CTP/EESR</p></li></ol><p class="MsoNormal">Key Deliverables :</p><ol><li><p>Ensuring discipline specific records (site wide) are captured in a timely manner, perform technical review &amp; address issues to support Area LTQR Coordinators processing area discipline LTQR deliverables</p></li><li><p>Responsible for Area Discipline LODs management, tracking asset installation and record verification and completion</p></li><li><p>To be familiar witch the Scope of Work, the Contract Specifications and appropriate Nuclear Sta,dards, the drawings and the procedures.</p></li><li><p>AS9 IWOC verification and track task completion upon A-Acceptance of LTQR deliverables in Teamcenter</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ol><p><strong><em>*LTQR</em></strong><em>s are one of the principal forms of objective evidence</em><span style="color:#474747"> for quality assurance and conformance inspection and testing.</span></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal">Mechanical Engineering or ONC/HNC/HND/C&amp;G/Recognised Apprenticeship in relevant discipline and Competency based assessment.</p><ol><li><p>Excellent IT skills and experience in applying electronic document management systems (edms) and associated metadata schemas.</p></li><li><p>Experience wording in a quality assurance/control environment within the nuclear industry or other relevant safety critical industry.</p></li><li><p>Proven experience of interaction and resolving issues with a wide range of stakeholders in a multi-cultural environnement</p></li><li><p>Major Project Experience</p></li><li><p>Nuclear Experience beneficial</p></li><li><p>Working in Alliance agreement projects</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tes/lead-mechanical-sector-nuclear-m-f-bridgwater-405192","tags":["Nuclear"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Bridgwater , Somerset, Royaume-Uni","created_at":1792323079},{"slug":"senior-cost-engineer-m-f-bridgwater-245543","company_name":"T.E.S","title":"Senior Cost Engineer (m/f)","description":"<p><strong>Technical Engineering Support</strong> (<strong>TES</strong>) is an engineering services company with over 30 years of experience, specializing in <strong>test</strong> coordination and industrial <strong>commissioning</strong>. TES also supports its clients in engineering <strong>studies</strong> and the <strong>assembly coordination</strong> of industrial equipment.</p><p>As part of our expanding activities on major infrastructure projects, we are currently looking for a <strong>Senior Cost Engineer (m/f)</strong> to serve as a technical lead within our project controls organization.</p><p>Acting as a subject matter expert within the <strong>Cost and Forecasting</strong> team for the Hinkley Point C (HPC) nuclear power station project, the Senior Cost Engineer ensures the uniform implementation of the cost management strategy across designated project areas. You will oversee the delivery of specific contracts ranging in value from <strong>£10m to £500m</strong>, direct the daily workload of Cost Engineers and Trainee Cost Engineers, and serve as the main face of cost management to Program Directors and key stakeholders.</p><p>This role actively underpins success across <strong>Engineering, Procurement &amp; Manufacturing, Construction, and Commissioning</strong> phases, aligning with HPC critical success factors:</p><ul><li><p>Integrated baseline delivery</p></li><li><p>EPC critical path execution</p></li><li><p>Key milestone achievement leading to Commercial Operation Date (COD)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Operating Environment Context:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Highly regulated context under the oversight of the <strong>Office for Nuclear Regulation (ONR)</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Deep integration of <strong>Nuclear Safety Culture</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Strict adherence to project priorities: <strong>Safety, Quality, Time, and Cost</strong>.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Key responsabilities :</strong> </p><ol><li><p><strong>Technical Leadership &amp; Team Guidance:</strong> Direct daily tasks and provide technical guidance to Cost Engineers and Trainee Cost Engineers. Lead training sessions on cost management software and processes for project management teams.</p></li><li><p><strong>Contract &amp; Data Management:</strong> Oversee cost and forecast data across high-value contract portfolios (£10m–£500m) in alignment with CBS/WBS. Ensure data integrity within systems such as <strong>EcoSys</strong> and <strong>SAP</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stakeholder Engagement &amp; Decision Support:</strong> Partner with Program/Area Directors to review major issues, lead scenario planning workshops, and present accurate insights at Board Meetings, Program Reviews, and ROTCS.</p></li><li><p><strong>Trend &amp; Risk Integration:</strong> Work alongside Risk Leads and Project Controls Managers to connect cost data with schedule, risk, and change management, ensuring high-quality risk information informs baseline estimates.</p></li><li><p><strong>Reporting &amp; Dashboards:</strong> Manage and verify data outputs within <strong>Power BI</strong> dashboards and ensure high-quality cost reporting across defined cycles.</p></li><li><p><strong>Governance &amp; Information Security:</strong> Support good governance, process enhancement, and strict compliance with protective marking for <strong>Sensitive Nuclear Information</strong>.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>Qualifications &amp; Experience Required:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Education:</strong> Minimum HND (or equivalent qualification/degree) in Project Management, Project Controls, Engineering, or a related field. Cost &amp; Forecasting specific qualifications are preferred.</p></li><li><p><strong>Experience:</strong> Minimum <strong>10 years of senior-level experience</strong> in a Cost and Forecasting role within a complex, highly regulated industry (energy, nuclear, major infrastructure).</p></li><li><p><strong>Expertise:</strong> Proven track record of managing multi-stakeholder interfaces, technical leadership, and active integration across project controls disciplines.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Direct experience on major complex construction projects.</p></li><li><p>Prior nuclear industry experience.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Software Tools</strong> :</p><h4><strong> </strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Software Expertise:</strong> Advanced user and trainer in <strong>EcoSys</strong>, <strong>SAP</strong>, <strong>Power BI</strong>, <strong>Teamcenter</strong>, and MS Office (Excel, Powerpoint, Access).</p></li><li><p><strong>Strategic &amp; Analytical Thinking:</strong> Ability to simplify complex financial and technical scenarios for executive-level audiences.</p></li><li><p><strong>Leadership:</strong> Strong delegation, coaching, interpersonal, and stakeholder-influencing capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tes/senior-cost-engineer-m-f-bridgwater-245543","tags":["Nuclear"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Bridgwater , Somerset, Royaume-Uni","created_at":1792323079},{"slug":"consultant-senior-consultant-financial-services-london-385327","company_name":"Delta Capita","title":"Consultant/Senior Consultant Financial Services","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW213903733 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Role - Consultant / Sr. Consultant</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Immediate Joiner</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Location - London (Hybrid)</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW213903733 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW213903733 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Role Summary</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">We are seeking a Consultant to support a major financial services transformation programme within a global banking environment. This role is suited to an early-career professional with strong stakeholder management, project coordination, operational improvement, and process optimisation experience. The successful candidate will work across business and technology teams, supporting change initiatives, operational enhancements, and project delivery activities.</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW213903733 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">The Role and Responsibilities</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><ol><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support delivery of business transformation and change initiatives across financial services operations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Coordinate with multiple stakeholders to ensure project milestones, actions, and dependencies are tracked effectively.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Gather, document, and maintain business requirements, process maps, and project documentation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Assist with operational reviews, process improvement activities, and workflow optimisation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support governance activities including status reporting, action tracking, and stakeholder communications.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Analyse operational data and prepare management information to support decision-making.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Facilitate workshops, meetings, and discussions with business and technology teams.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support user adoption, training, and change management activities.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Identify risks, issues, and bottlenecks and escalate appropriately.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to continuous improvement initiatives using automation and AI-enabled solutions where applicable.</span></p></li></ol> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW115606457 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Required Experience:</span></strong></p><ol><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience working within financial services, banking, insurance, consulting, or a regulated environment.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Exposure to project coordination, business change, transformation, operations, or process improvement initiatives.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong stakeholder management and communication skills.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience working across multiple teams and managing competing priorities.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ability to analyse processes and identify opportunities for operational efficiency.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong organisational skills and attention to detail.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Comfortable producing reports, presentations, and project documentation.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ol><p class="Paragraph SCXW115606457 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desired Experience :</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115606457 BCX8"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Exposure to business transformation, project management, or consulting engagements.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of investment banking, capital markets, or financial services operations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience supporting change management or user adoption initiatives.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with automation, AI tools, or workflow optimisation projects.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with Agile delivery methodologies.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Skills &amp; Tools :</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, PowerPoint, Word)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Jira</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Power BI</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Process documentation and workflow mapping</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Data analysis and reporting</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong presentation and stakeholder engagement skills</span></p></li></ul><h3></h3><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Candidate Profile :</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Early-career consultant with strong potential to develop within finan