ts.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This is a pure new business role focused on identifying opportunities, creating a pipeline and converting prospects into long-term partnerships : Your key role will be to identify opportunities, engage decision-makers and position Eco Counter as the preferred partner for mobility data solutions :</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Working with the General Manager to develop and deliver New Business Development strategies which identify and target new business opportunities within the Active Travel and Transport market and exposes the Eco-Counter organisation to prospective new clients</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Drive new business development through proactive outreach methodology, professional presentation with swift responses to created opportunities</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Win new business by developing a strong understanding of client needs, identifying and recommending the most suitable Eco-Counter solutions which exceed client requirements and deliver long term recurring revenue.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">Engage with and meet decision-makers in cities, counties, national parks, and other public bodies – building long term relationships and becoming their trusted solution expert to ensure Eco Counter solutions are always their preferred choice</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Attend industry events, conferences to develop market knowledge, competitor activity and network decision makers to monitor and report on industry regulations, government incentives, and new technologies.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Provide support throughout the business development lifecycle, from initial client interaction to deal support and documentation.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Participate in industry events, trade shows, and conferences to gather market intelligence and support brand presence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">A real sales “<strong>Hunter</strong>” with a passion for delivering new sales and driving exceptional customer experience</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Someone who “Loves the thrill of the chase” with excellent ability to explain <strong>technical concepts</strong> in a clear and accessible way</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Someone who will go the “extra mile” with an “ABC” mindset and sales approach with a demonstrable track record in successful <strong>NBD sales roles</strong></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><strong>5-10 years experience</strong> of working in the Public sector with a strong interest in active transportation, sustainability, or public space planning and established contacts in the urban or nature sectors would be a real positive</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">If you have the above Sales Skill set and experience of the <strong>Active Travel,</strong> Transport and <strong>Road Safety sectors</strong> and how these impact a Greener, Safer and Heathier environment you could be an ideal candidate</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Willingness to travel across UK with occasional international visits</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>About You</strong></p><p>You are someone who:</p><ul><li><p>Enjoys <strong>prospecting and opening new doors</strong></p></li><li><p>Is motivated by <strong>building a pipeline from scratch</strong></p></li><li><p>Thrives in a <strong>target-driven environment</strong></p></li><li><p>Is curious, persistent and relationship-oriented</p></li><li><p>Can engage confidently with <strong>senior public sector stakeholders</strong></p></li><li><p>Is comfortable working independently while collaborating with internal teams</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Has a strong communicator with excellent interpersonal and presentation skills</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">Comfortable using CRM and Sales performance tools to accurately report on activity, build and deliver from a pipeline</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The opportunity to join an innovative international company with a meaningful global mission with demonstrable growth &amp; profitability</p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A supportive and collaborative work environment with an open people and trusting culture</p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Opportunities for professional development and travel</p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Competitive salary and benefits (to be discussed based on ability and experience)</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/eco-compteur/remote-senior-new-business-sales-manager-active-travel-smart-mobility-silverstone-259589","tags":["TRAFFIC TECHNOLOGY","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Poste à distance","created_at":1792323074},{"slug":"leadership-personal-growth-consultant-danehill-67703","company_name":"RiseBeyond.Today","title":"Leadership & Personal Growth Consultant","description":"<h2>About the job</h2><p>Are you looking for greater flexibility, personal growth and purpose in the next chapter of your career?</p><p>Perhaps you’ve built a successful career in Talent - Acquisition or Recruiting, Learning & Development, Consulting, Sales, Business Development or another professional field.</p><p>Now you’re beginning to ask different questions about what comes next.</p><h2>About the Position</h2><p>RiseBeyond.Today works alongside an established global organisation specialising in personal growth and leadership development.</p><p>We’re looking to connect with experienced, growth-minded professionals who enjoy learning, building meaningful relationships and helping others realise their potential.</p><p>This flexible remote position offers comprehensive training, ongoing support and the opportunity to continue developing yourself while making a positive impact on others.</p><p>This isn’t simply about changing jobs. It’s about thinking differently about what’s possible for the next chapter of your career and your life.</p><h2>What You’ll Be Doing</h2><ul><li>Conducting professional online conversations</li><li>Building authentic relationships</li><li>Connecting with individuals seeking personal and professional growth</li><li>Leveraging proven digital marketing strategies and online tools</li><li>Participating in ongoing learning and mentoring</li></ul><h2>Who We’re Looking For</h2><p>Professionals from backgrounds such as:</p><ul><li>Leadership & Management</li><li>HR or Talent Acquisition</li><li>Learning & Development</li><li>Recruitment & Executive Search</li><li>Consulting & Professional Services</li><li>Business Development & Sales</li></ul><p>Applicants should have a minimum of 5 years’ professional or corporate experience.</p><p>Mindset matters more than job title.</p><p>We’re looking for people who are excited by what’s possible rather than limited by what’s familiar.</p><p>You’ll thrive if you:</p><ul><li>Have a growth mindset and enjoy continual learning</li><li>Think beyond traditional career paths</li><li>Are curious about new possibilities</li><li>Are self-motivated and accountable</li><li>Build strong relationships</li><li>Enjoy helping others succeed</li><li>Think beyond the next twelve months and are excited by what could be possible over the next five to ten years</li></ul><p>This position resonates most strongly with ambitious, open-minded people committed to continual personal and professional growth.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul><li>Flexible hours (part-time or full-time)</li><li>Remote working</li><li>Comprehensive onboarding, training and mentoring</li><li>Ongoing personal and professional development</li><li>Proven digital marketing strategies and online tools</li><li>Performance-based compensation</li></ul><p>Perhaps you’re looking for:</p><ul><li>More flexibility and autonomy</li><li>Greater or continued personal and professional growth</li><li>New challenges and opportunities</li><li>Work that aligns more closely with your values and aspirations</li></ul><h2>Important Information</h2><p>This is an Independent Contractor position and is not a salaried employment role.</p><p>Compensation is performance-based and aligned with individual activity and results.</p><h2>Ready to Explore?</h2><p>We’d love to hear from you if you’re passionate about learning, growth and helping people realise their potential.</p><p>Apply today. Following an initial review, suitable applicants will be invited to a brief discovery call.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/risebeyondtoday/leadership-personal-growth-consultant-danehill-67703","tags":["Remote","Training","Development"],"job_types":["Freelancer / indepedent contractor","freelance","professional / experienced"],"location":"Danehill","created_at":1792319465},{"slug":"product-manager-homepage-london-174348","company_name":"wolt","title":"Product Manager, Homepage","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Join us in shaping the experience that millions of customers land on every time they open DoorDash, Wolt, or Deliveroo. As part of our Core Consumer organisation, our Homepage team owns one of the single biggest levers we have on what customers find and one of the hardest surfaces in the app to get right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at the intersection of ranking, personalisation, and AI/ML, you&#39;ll help decide what each customer sees and why, across three brands and dozens of markets. You&#39;ll be building on a global stack, and your roadmap will be a mix: global platform problems that apply worldwide, global capabilities we&#39;re accelerating into EMEA, and EMEA-specific problems worth solving properly rather than working around.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Product Manager to join our Homepage team. In this role, you&#39;ll shape how customers discover restaurants, grocery and retail venues, dishes and products — and help define what discovery looks like as AI-driven and agentic experiences change the way people decide what to order.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining a team working on one of the most-used surfaces in the app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s what your day-to-day might look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building new end-to-end features and user experiences on Homepage that shape how customers discover restaurants, grocery and retail venues, dishes, and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on ranking, personalisation, and AI/ML problems in the Homepage domain, including how we decide what each customer sees and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring where AI-driven and agentic experiences change the way customers discover what to order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making discovery work across three brands and many markets, without flattening into one-size-fits-all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ideal candidate will bring strong product judgment and curiosity to grow into the rest:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Product Manager on consumer-facing products - discovery, homepage, feed, or ranking-driven experiences are especially relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a product manager more than a feature owner. Someone who finds the customer problems that matter most and makes the case for solving them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work backwards from the customer problem, and weigh it against what the business needs most right now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable holding several business objectives at once and making a call when they pull in different directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well with a wide range of stakeholders and build trust with people whose priorities differ from your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically and can move between long-term direction and what we should ship next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity and genuinely flexible (this industry is changing fast, AI most of all).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about what AI actually changes for customers, and can tell real value from hype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Next steps&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position will be filled as soon as we find the right person, so make sure to apply as soon as you realize you really, really want to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ncz4s_oBczc?si=FzuwoSOLcv5WZVRN&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wolt/product-manager-homepage-london-174348","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792313718},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-london-323413","company_name":"smartsheet","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 20 years, Smartsheet has empowered teams to manage work seamlessly and scale solutions smarter. Now, in our most ambitious chapter yet, we are uniting human teams with AI agents. By orchestrating the work agents do best, automating manual tasks and uncovering insights at scale, we create the space for people to focus on what truly matters: judgment, creativity, and big thinking. That is magic at work, and it’s what we show up for every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Smartsheet is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; to join our EMEA organisation. You will be responsible for increasing software and services sales by expanding existing customers&#39; adoption along with targeting new logo acquisition. This is an incredibly exciting opportunity to help build out a strategically important vertical for Smartsheet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based at Smartsheet in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;London, UK (hybrid or UK, remote eligible)&lt;/strong&gt; and reports to a &lt;strong&gt;Regional Director, Enterprise Sales.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed quarterly and annual software and services sales quotas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead primary and secondary account teams by partnering with Solution Engineering, Consulting, Customer Success, Customer Outcomes, Marketing and Sales Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop short and long-term growth and renewal strategies across your customer base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance tactical execution whilst ultimately targeting complex, high-value solution-based deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively develop unsolicited proposals that align with customer initiatives and position Smartsheet as an enterprise software solution provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately forecast sales opportunities, while tracking and using critical metrics that predict sales success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience selling enterprise software or services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of exceeding assigned quotas and receiving recognition for high-performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience building relationships with senior line-of-business leaders, IT executives and operational managers within Enterprise organisations (&amp;gt;10,000 employees)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding and experience of selling directly and through partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a large and diverse pipeline of sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in developing successful go-to-market strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience executing complex, solution-based strategic sales processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;World class sales basics in terms of pipe generation approaches, territory planning, account planning and deal execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly accountable for actions and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and adaptable to change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity with the ability to build trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent instinct and judgment to make sound choices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self awareness in terms of strengths, weaknesses and where to have the highest impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in ambiguity with the ability to translate complexity into clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High humility with a mindset of continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, creative and able to respectfully challenge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and driven by a need to make a difference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides leadership by leveraging collective strengths, providing vision and by buying into collective objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legally eligible to work in the UK on an ongoing basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid Private Medical and Dental, additional cost for family members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly contributions toward your pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly stipend to support your work and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid for Holiday + Bank Holidays + Flexible Time Away Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 weeks fully paid Maternity Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks fully paid Paternity/Adoption Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal paid Volunteer Day to support our community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for professional growth and development including access to Udemy online courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Funded Perks including a counseling membership, salary sacrifice options, and your own personal Smartsheet account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teleworking options from any registered location in the UK (role specific)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Smartsheet, your ideas are heard, your potential is supported, and your contributions have real impact. You’ll have the freedom to explore, push boundaries, and grow beyond your role. We welcome diverse perspectives and nontraditional paths—because we know that impact comes from individuals who care deeply and challenge thoughtfully. When you’re doing work that stretches you, excites you, and connects you to something bigger, that’s magic at work. Let’s build what’s next, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartsheet is an Equal Opportunity (EEO) employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment with the best employees. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable laws in the US, UK, Australia, Germany, Costa Rica, Japan, Bulgaria, India, and Singapore. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there are preparations we can make to help ensure you have a comfortable and positive interview experience, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/smartsheet/enterprise-account-executive-london-323413","tags":["Large Enterprise Reps"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792313715},{"slug":"product-marketing-lead-emea-london-273141","company_name":"Vanta","title":"Product Marketing Lead - EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Vanta, our mission is to help businesses earn and prove trust.<strong> </strong>We believe that security should be monitored and verified continuously, and we empower companies to practice better security and prove it with ease. Vanta has a kind and talented team, and while some have prior security experience, many have been successful at Vanta without it. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a product marketer at Vanta, you’ll help bring this vision to life by defining the new category of trust management, shaping Vanta’s positioning and differentiators externally, and influencing our product and business roadmap. We sit at the intersection of Marketing &amp; Demand Generation, Sales, Product, and Customer Success and revel in connecting all of these teams to drive the business forward. Research, analysis, curiosity, storytelling, and project management are just a few of the attributes of our team – in addition to being open, empathetic, and genuinely nice people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the EMEA Product Marketing lead, you will be responsible for bringing Vanta’s story to the EMEA audience to help us drive sustainable growth in the market. You’ll craft compelling messaging that’s tailored to the region, based on insights from buyer and market research. You’ll lead product launches to help amplify Vanta’s presence in the region, and partner closely with our product management team to identify growth opportunities for us to continue building our product. Finally, you’ll partner closely with our GTM organisation to expand Vanta’s footprint and accelerate our growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do as a Product Marketing Lead at Vanta:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and manage go-to-market (GTM) strategy for Vanta’s business in EMEA tailored to the unique opportunities across the EMEA region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop tailored messaging and positioning for EMEA based on market research and customer insights</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with our EMEA growth team on the development and execution of targeted marketing campaigns, including tailored messaging and content that effectively engage local audiences and drive business objectives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and execute large product launches (including GTM enablement of sales and customer success), report back on performance, and optimize our launch processes for scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Author compelling content for each stage of the customer journey, from blog posts to sales collateral</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talk regularly to Vanta’s customers, analyze your own data, and understand our competitive landscape to help shape the product strategy and roadmap and inform Vanta’s overall EMEA marketing strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with the EMEA team at Vanta – including demand gen, sales, customer success, and product—to help achieve our objectives in the market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Refine Vanta’s pricing and packaging based on deep insights around the market, our product value, and customer needs in partnership with finance, operations, product, sales, and customer success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be a strong customer champion, creative marketer, and problem solver</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How to be successful in this role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have 7+ years of Product Marketing experience, with an emphasis on B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a deep empathy for users and an ability to adapt communication to best reach, engage and differentiate Vanta to your audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy working with data and pairing those quantitative conclusions with the qualitative conversations you have with users</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find delight in understanding how things work and then explaining your newfound knowledge to others</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must be based on London or Dublin, this role will be hybrid in-office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open to using AI to amplify their skills and strengthen their work - demonstrating curiosity, a willingness to learn, and sound judgment in applying AI responsibly to improve efficiency and impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can expect as a Vanta’n:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Industry-competitive salary and equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">100% covered medical, dental, and vision benefits with dependents coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">16 weeks paid Parental Leave for all new parents Health &amp; wellness stipend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote workspace, internet, and mobile phone stipend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuter benefits for team members who attend the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension matching</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of Annual Leave per year and unlimited sick time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8 company-paid holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Virtual team building activities, lunch and learns, and other company-wide events!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in SF, NYC, London, Dublin, Tel Aviv, and Sydney</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-hybrid</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Vanta, we are committed to hiring diverse talent of different backgrounds and as such, it is important to us to provide an inclusive work environment for all. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, gender identity, age, religion, sexual orientation, veteran or disability status, or any other protected class. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage and welcome people of all backgrounds to apply.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Vanta</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in 2018, in the wake of several high-profile data breaches. Online security was only becoming more important, but we knew firsthand how hard it could be for fast-growing companies to invest the time and manpower it takes to build a solid security foundation. Vanta was inspired by a vision to restore trust in internet businesses by enabling companies to improve and prove their security. From our early days automating security monitoring for compliance standards like SOC 2, HIPAA and ISO 27001 to creating the world's leading Trust Management Platform, our vision remains unchanged. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now more than ever, making security continuous—not just a point-in-time check— is essential. Thousands of companies rely on Vanta to build, maintain and demonstrate their trust— all in a way that's real-time and transparent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Referral Instructions</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/vanta/product-marketing-lead-emea-london-273141","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1792312822},{"slug":"managing-director-uk-london-444328","company_name":"Everfield","title":"Managing Director, UK","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong>: United Kingdom</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Type:</strong> Full-time | Hybrid-flexible | Based near one of our portfolio company locations</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Note</strong>: This is an ongoing opportunity for future Managing Directors across the Everfield ecosystem. As we continue to grow our portfolio, we are proactively engaging with candidates who have the leadership experience and operational expertise to step into Managing Director roles within our vertical market software companies.</p><h2><br /><strong>About Everfield</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield buys, builds, and grows European vertical market and specialist software companies, providing them with the tools they need to move to the next level. Our mission is to foster ambition, fuel growth, and unlock opportunities for Europe’s software ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Companies in the Everfield ecosystem follow a decentralised model, maintaining their team, brand, and offices while focusing on what they do best—building products and supporting customers. Everfield provides support in talent acquisition, HR, and access to a team of experts in building and growing European B2B SaaS companies who consult on financial and operational topics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Founded in 2022, Everfield has an ecosystem presence in 7 countries—and growing.</p><h2><br /><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Managing Director (MD), you will lead one of Everfield’s portfolio companies and assume full ownership of its strategy, execution, and performance. This role is designed for operationally strong leaders with deep experience in software businesses who are ready to take end-to-end responsibility for a growing company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You will work closely with Everfield’s central teams but operate independently, with the autonomy to shape the future of the business. This role is especially suited to individuals with prior experience running software companies in a standalone or platform model, particularly in the €2M–€10M recurring revenue range.</p><h2><br /><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><br /><strong>Strategic Vision &amp; Growth</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and execute long-term strategy, aligned with scalable growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify new market opportunities, product innovations, and partnerships</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor competitive trends to position the business effectively</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Leadership &amp; Influence</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, develop, and retain high-performing cross-functional teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inspire cultural alignment and ownership across the organization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion team effectiveness and collaboration while serving as a coach and decision-maker</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Financial Acumen</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead financial planning, forecasting, and reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage full P&amp;L and own key performance metrics (EBITDA, ARR, MRR)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive revenue growth and cost optimization to achieve financial targets</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Commercial Execution</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the go-to-market model, including sales, marketing, and pricing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear KPIs and performance systems to track revenue and funnel efficiency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive customer retention and recurring revenue growth</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Communication &amp; Stakeholder Management</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the company externally and internally with investors, partners, and customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report to Everfield’s central team with strategic and financial updates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the face of the business while cultivating lasting external relationships</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Operational Excellence</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve internal operations, product delivery, and support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement systems and processes for scalable growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive a culture of operational discipline and innovation</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Candidate Profile</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are especially interested in individuals with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience as a Managing Director, General Manager, or CEO in a B2B software or SaaS environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success leading a business with €2M–€10M in recurring revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full accountability for business performance, including P&amp;L, headcount, and strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with multi-site or multi-entity software company structures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience operating within decentralised models or working with shared-service or platform support functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on leadership style, grounded in operational excellence, clear communication, and cultural stewardship</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Who Should Apply</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome interest from experienced software leaders who understand the dynamics of buy-and-hold environments and portfolio-driven growth—particularly those who have thrived in <strong>aggregator</strong>, <strong>accumulator</strong>, or <strong>roll-up</strong> software organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While we review each application carefully, we are currently focused on candidates who bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First-hand experience scaling vertical or niche software businesses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with decentralized ownership and platform-based acquisition models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A desire to take full accountability for a business and build for the long term</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>If this context resonates and your experience aligns, we’d love to hear from you.</em></p><h2><br /><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> Lead and grow a business with full strategic and operational ownership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support:</strong> Access to Everfield’s network of functional experts and peers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth:</strong> Potential to take on broader leadership within Everfield over time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Community:</strong> Be part of a long-term, values-driven ecosystem of software entrepreneurs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility:</strong> Hybrid working across key European markets with in-person collaboration</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Note on Timing</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">While we may not have an immediate opening in your geography or vertical, we maintain a high-touch pipeline of senior candidates aligned with our investment roadmap.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates with the experience outlined above will be contacted for follow-up discussions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are an equal opportunity employer and ensure that no applicant is subject to less favourable treatment on the grounds of gender, gender identity, marital status, race, colour, nationality, ethnicity, age, sexual orientation, socio-economic, responsibilities for dependants, physical or mental disability. Any hiring decision are made on the basis of skills, qualifications and experiences.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/everfield/managing-director-uk-london-444328","tags":["Everfield HQ"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK - Remote","created_at":1792312820},{"slug":"member-experience-training-quality-specialist-uk-london-185293","company_name":"Neko Health","title":"Member Experience Training & Quality Specialist - UK","description":"<h3><strong>Mission</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neko is redefining what prevention means, from treating illness when it arrives, to sustaining health before it's ever at risk. Our mission: make data-driven, preventative care accessible to more people, before symptoms appear. <br /><br />In a single, non-invasive visit under an hour, proprietary technology and direct clinical care combine to deliver personalised, actionable insights. It's a team that thinks in 10x, not 10%. Every role here plays a part in building a world where prevention is the norm, and where your work genuinely helps people live longer, healthier lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Purpose</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Member Experience Training &amp; Quality Specialist makes the Neko member experience standard real on the ground. You deliver our member experience training to teams across the business, primarily clinic teams and centralised support teams, and you run the quality assurance activity that tells us whether the standard is actually landing in practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a delivery role at the heart of a live culture change programme. You will facilitate training that shifts mindset, not just process, run experience audits against CARE and the Member First Manifesto, and turn what you see into coaching and improvement. As markets scale, you keep the standard consistent across every site and cohort, and rising over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the coordination and logistics that keep training and quality assurance running: scheduling sessions and audits, and organising the people, spaces and materials each one needs. You report to the Hospitality Programme Lead and support the wider rollout, so you will also play a hands-on part in projects and launch activity as new clinics and teams come online.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Deliver in the First 6–12 Months</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 1 and Stage 2 member experience training delivered consistently to every new clinic cohort in your market, with 30-day reviews showing the mindset shift is landing, not just attendance being logged. <em>(Member First, always)</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A regular quality assurance rhythm is live: experience audits across clinic and support teams, scored consistently against CARE and the Member First Manifesto, with clear findings shared back to the teams and their leads. <em>(Impact, not activity)</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Audit insight turned into action: recurring friction points named early and at least two concrete experience improvements implemented with clinic and support leads. <em>(Optimistic truth-seeking)</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support team training built out and delivered alongside clinic training, so centralised member support holds the same standard as the clinic floor. <em>(Chase 10X, not 10%)</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ongoing learning ecosystem running smoothly, including the monthly AI role play and quiz, with completion tracked and shared with Clinic Leads as a coaching tool, not a performance measure. <em>(Tech-enabled, human-centred)</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A training and audit calendar owned end to end: sessions scheduled around clinic rotas and cohort timing, facilitators, rooms, materials and joining details arranged, and audits planned on a set cadence so every site and team is covered without gaps. <em>(Impact, not activity)</em><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in training delivery, learning and development, hospitality, or member and customer experience, ideally in a high-touch service, hospitality, or premium retail environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A confident facilitator, comfortable leading a room of clinicians and operators and holding attention and energy across a full-day session.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience running quality assurance or experience audits, mystery shopping, or service standard reviews, with the ability to score consistently and give feedback that changes behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A sharp eye for service detail and what separates a good experience from an exceptional one, drawn from service design and hospitality thinking rather than process alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organised and self-directed, able to run a training and audit calendar across multiple sites and cohorts without dropping the standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication, and the credibility to influence teams and leads who do not report to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel regularly between clinic sites, and occasionally between markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting a multi-site clinic, hospitality, or retail rollout as it scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with digital learning tools, an LMS, or AI-enabled training and assessment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident with everyday workplace tools, including Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Excel and Outlook, to build training materials, track audits and report findings.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Process</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates progress from application and structured screening through thoughtfully designed interviews culminating in a formal offer and final pre-employment checks before joining the team.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunity &amp; Inclusion Statement</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neko Health is committed to inclusive hiring and member-first care. We welcome candidates from all backgrounds and encourage you to request reasonable adjustments to support your application.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/neko-health/member-experience-training-quality-specialist-uk-london-185293","tags":["Operations & Markets"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792312820},{"slug":"staff-ai-deployment-strategist-uk-nordics-london-29771","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Staff AI Deployment Strategist - UK & Nordics","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Staff AI Deployment Strategist</strong>, you will shape how some of the most ambitious enterprises in the UK &amp; Nordics region adopt frontier AI at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior, high-impact role at the intersection of strategy, technology, and execution. You will work directly on Mistral’s most strategic opportunities and largest deliveries, helping customers move from ambition to measurable business outcomes. You will frame complex AI transformation programs, turn executive priorities into actionable roadmaps, and ensure that Mistral delivers systems that are valuable, scalable, and trusted.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also act as a senior sponsor on our most critical customer programs, bringing judgment, structure, and delivery excellence to high-stakes engagements. Your mandate is to raise th