":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ballys-intralot-sa/lead-ai-engineer-manchester-228337","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Manchester, Manchester, United Kingdom","created_at":1792312290},{"slug":"head-of-product-marketing-management-london-226739","company_name":"UpSlide","title":"Head of Product Marketing Management  (London)","description":"<p style="text-align:start;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://upslide.com/">UpSlide</a> <span style="color:#121317">is the </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">document production layer for financial services</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">We orchestrate LLMs, machine learning, and workflow agents within Microsoft 365 to deliver </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">reliable, quality outputs </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">in the most efficient and cost-effective way. As a</span><strong><span style="color:#121317"> Microsoft Solutions Partner</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, with 14+ years supporting financial services teams, we bring together </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">expertise from the tech, finance and design fields</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> to help clients like KPMG, BNP Paribas, Rothschild &amp; Co. </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">boost productivity while improving brand consistency</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> across their corporate documents.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">We are a </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">certified B Corporation</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, upholding the belief that businesses should have a positive impact on society.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Our values ✨</span></strong></h4><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Our values guide our approach to work and are at the heart of our recruitment process. To join our team, we look for individuals who value:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Excellence:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> </span><em><span style="color:#121317">We think that every detail counts, and we place great importance on the quality of our deliverables.</span></em></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Trust:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> </span><em><span style="color:#121317">We are passionate, committed, and free to act with autonomy.</span></em></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Happiness at work:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> </span><em><span style="color:#121317">We enjoy looking on the bright side and we share our enthusiasm with our colleagues and clients.</span></em></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong>The team 🧑‍🤝‍🧑</strong></h4><p>UpSlide is a productivity platform for Microsoft 365 (PowerPoint, Excel and Word) built for financial professionals in investment banking, private equity, asset management and advisory. Product Marketing sits at the centre of Product, Sales and Marketing: we decide how UpSlide is positioned, priced and sold.</p><p>You'll join as our Head of Product Marketing, reporting directly to <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/matteobordin2/">Matteo Bordin</a>, our Chief Product Officer.</p><p>You'll manage one PMM and over time grow your team.</p><p>Day-to-day, you'll work closely with Sales, Product, and Marketing leadership. This is a hands-on leadership role: you'll <strong>set direction and still get into the work.</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong>Team goals 🎯</strong></h4><p>Product Marketing's job is to make UpSlide easy to understand, easy to sell, and priced right. Concretely, that means:</p><ul><li><p>Sharpen positioning and messaging so prospects grasp the value fast.</p></li><li><p>Arm Sales to win, especially against direct competitors.</p></li><li><p>Own pricing and packaging decisions and the reasoning behind them.</p></li><li><p>Run customer communications that drive adoption and expansion.</p></li></ul><p>The impact on the business is direct: higher win rates, stronger pricing power, shorter sales cycles.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong>Your responsibilities 🖋️</strong></h4><p><strong>Positioning &amp; narrative (25%)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Own UpSlide's positioning and messaging across segments and personas.</p></li><li><p>Turn product capabilities into a clear story that resonates with financial professionals.</p></li><li><p>Keep messaging consistent across the website, sales materials and campaigns.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Sales enablement &amp; competitive intelligence (25%)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Build the enablement that helps Sales qualify, pitch and close: decks, battlecards, objection handling and one-pagers.</p></li><li><p>Own competitive intelligence: track competitors, brief the business, keep our differentiation sharp.</p></li><li><p>Partner with Sales leadership on win/loss analysis and act on what it tells you.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Pricing &amp; packaging (20%)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Own pricing and packaging: structure, tiers, and the logic behind them.</p></li><li><p>Run the analysis and make clear recommendations to the exec team.</p></li><li><p>Support Sales on deal-level pricing and commercial strategy.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Customer communications (15%)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Own how we communicate with customers: launches, releases and lifecycle comms.</p></li><li><p>Drive adoption and expansion through clear, well-timed messaging.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Team leadership (15%)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Lead, coach, and grow the PMM you’ll manage.</p></li><li><p>Set priorities and hold a high bar on output.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong>Your goals ⚡</strong></h4><p><strong>First 3 months</strong>: Learn the product, customers and competitors in depth. Build relationships with Sales and Product. Audit our current positioning, pricing and enablement, and tell us where the gaps are.</p><p><strong>By 6 months</strong>: Ship a refreshed positioning and messaging framework. Stand up a repeatable competitive intelligence rhythm. Deliver a first pricing and packaging recommendation.</p><p><strong>By 9 months</strong>: Have an enablement program running that measurably improves win rates, pricing changes live or in flight, and a customer communications cadence the business relies on.</p><p>As UpSlide grows, this role can grow into broader marketing leadership. We'll back you to get there.</p> <br> <p><strong>You are a great fit if you have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Significant experience in <strong>enterprise B2B sales</strong>: you've either carried a quota in complex, high-value deals or worked hand in hand with sellers who do. This is a must.</p></li><li><p>A proven product marketing track record: positioning, messaging and sales enablement that moved the needle.</p></li><li><p>Experience owning or heavily influencing <strong>pricing and packaging</strong> decisions.</p></li><li><p>People leadership experience: you've managed and developed marketers.</p></li><li><p>Excellent written and verbal communication in English, and the judgement to write for an exec audience.</p></li></ul><p><strong>We'd love it if:</strong></p><ul><li><p>You've worked in or sold to <strong>financial services</strong>: investment banking, private equity, asset management, or advisory. </p></li><li><p>You know the Microsoft 365 / productivity software space.</p></li><li><p>You speak French (not mandatory)<br></p></li></ul><p><em>✨ If you don't tick all the boxes but you think you'd be a great fit, please apply and tell us why.</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Recruitment process</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>First screening</strong> with our Talent Acquisition team (30 to 45 min, phone or video): mutual fit and motivation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Manager interview</strong> with Matteo Bordin, CPO (45 min to 1h30, video or in person): product thinking and experience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Peer interview</strong> with a peer from Product, Marketing, and Sales (~45 min).</p></li><li><p><strong>Case study</strong> with Matteo and a Product peer (45 min to 1h30): a deeper problem worked through together.</p></li></ul><p><em>🚀 We'll conduct a reference check to learn how to help you thrive!</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>What we offer</strong></h3><p>🌍&nbsp;<strong>International environment:</strong>&nbsp;Start-up with five offices (Paris, London, Berlin, New York, Singapore) and users in more than 60 countries</p><p>🌱&nbsp;<strong>Training &amp; professional development:</strong>&nbsp;Collaboration with our sister company, <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.potentiels-humains.com/">IPH</a>, which provides UpSliders with training on key soft skills and management</p><p>🎉&nbsp;<strong>Company events:</strong>&nbsp;Office socials and international company events (e.g. annual company seminar, team seminar, and sustainability actions taken throughout the year)</p><p><strong>🏠 Beautiful office:</strong>&nbsp;An inspiring eighth-floor corner office near Liverpool Street with beautiful common areas and meeting rooms, a balcony with a view, bike storage and showers, tea/coffee, etc.</p><p>💻&nbsp;<strong>Hybrid work:</strong>&nbsp;3 days in-office per week</p><p>🧑‍💻 <strong>Work-from-home budget:</strong> €500 WFH equipment budget</p><p>⏰ <strong>Flexi-work:</strong> Flex your schedule however works (e.g. bank hours across the fortnight to take a Friday off)</p><p>💆‍♀️&nbsp;<strong>Wellness package:</strong>&nbsp;£45 per month for physical and mental wellness activities</p><p>👶&nbsp;<strong>Family support:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Paid parental leave for birthing and non-birthing parents</p></li><li><p>4 days fully paid leave for sick children up to 6 years old or up to €1,800 for childcare reimbursement</p></li><li><p>Flexible return to work options</p></li><li><p>An additional 5 days are fully paid within 6 months after becoming a parent</p></li></ul><p>✈&nbsp;<strong>Holidays:</strong>&nbsp;25 days plus public holidays &amp; a half-day of additional holiday per year of full service (up to 5 additional days)</p><p><strong>🪙&nbsp;Pension:</strong> Pension contributions (with matched contributions up to 5% after one year)</p><p>🩺 <strong>Health insurance:</strong> Opportunity to opt into a health insurance plan (Vitality)</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317">As a B Corp-certified company, we have strong commitments toward our employees, community, clients, suppliers, and the environment. We strive to create an environment where everyone feels welcome. This commitment to diversity and inclusion is applied in our recruitment process and your employee experience once you’ve joined UpSlide ✨</span></em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/upslide/head-of-product-marketing-management-london-226739","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Senior manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, England, United Kingdom","created_at":1792312288},{"slug":"senior-rust-developer-london-483441","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior Rust Developer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;">We are seeking a skilled Core Developer (Rust/&nbsp;C++) for Swarm Robotics &amp; Sensor Control&nbsp;with over 5 years of professional experience to join our new development team in London. You will play a key role in building and optimizing the core architectures for the real-time control and management of robotic swarms and sensor systems. This position offers the opportunity to work with cutting-edge technologies and contribute to complex, mission-critical systems in a collaborative environment.</p><p style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Design, develop, and maintain robust and scalable systems for swarm control and sensor management.</p></li><li><p>Implement efficient communication protocols and real-time processing solutions for robotics.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate closely with cross-functional teams to integrate backend components with robotics software and sensor networks.</p></li><li><p>Optimize system performance, scalability, and reliability in a distributed robotics environment.</p></li><li><p>Solve challenging problems using modern programming languages such as <strong>C++</strong> and <strong>Rust</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Participate in code reviews, architecture discussions, and software design decisions.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>5+ years of professional experience in backend development with a strong focus on real-time systems.</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in <strong>C++</strong> and <strong>Rust</strong>, with a solid understanding of modern software development practices.</p></li><li><p>Experience in building and optimizing backend architectures for distributed systems.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with network protocols, multithreading, and low-latency data processing.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of system architecture design, performance optimization, and resource management.</p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently, solve complex technical problems, and thrive in a fast-paced startup environment.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice-to-Have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience in robotics, swarm control, or sensor integration.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with cloud platforms, Docker, or Kubernetes for scalable deployments.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of embedded systems or real-time operating environments.</p></li></ul><p><br></p><h4><strong>Why Quantum-Systems:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>We believe in the power of combined&nbsp;efforts: straightforward tech expertise&nbsp;paired with a customer-centric focus.</p></li><li><p>We are industry pioneers&nbsp;who are ambitious, bold,&nbsp;and visionary. </p></li><li><p>We push limits, think&nbsp;outside-the-box and strive&nbsp;for technological excellence to&nbsp;shape the future of aerial data.</p></li><li><p>We promise to be your runway&nbsp;for individual and professional&nbsp;growth.</p></li></ul><p><strong><br></strong></p><h4><strong>Our benefits:</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Company pension scheme: </strong>We support you so that you can already make provisions for later.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible working hours: </strong>With trust-based working hours, you are not only responsible for your working hours, but also for your work-life balance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile working: </strong>If it gets too turbulent for you in our office, you can get the necessary balance through mobile working.</p></li><li><p><strong>Bike-Leasing: </strong>We support you in staying environmentally mobile and healthy.</p></li><li><p><strong>Corporate Benefits: </strong>Your opportunity for attractive offers and discounts from well-known suppliers and brands, e.g. Adidas, Apple, Expedia.</p></li><li><p><strong>Employee events: </strong>We not only want to grow together, but also celebrate our successes together.</p></li></ul><p><br></p><h4><strong>About us:</strong></h4><p style="text-align:justify;">Quantum Systems specialises in the development, design, and production of small Unmanned Aerial Systems (sUAS). The company’s range of electric vertical take-off and landing (eVTOL) sUAS are built to maximize range and versatility and to provide operators with a seamless user experience. By integrating cutting-edge software capabilities, like edge computing and real-time AI-powered data processing, Quantum Systems is building next-generation UAS for clients in defence, security, public sectors.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><iframe height="281" width="500" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/_tjzWB0ttBM"></iframe></figure><p><br></p><h4><strong>Our commitment:</strong></h4><p>We are an open-minded company that not only values diversity, but actively promotes it. Regardless of gender, age, ethnic origin, religion, sexual orientation or disability, we firmly believe that the diversity of our employees is an essential part of our success.</p><p>At our company, every voice is heard and every perspective is valued. We believe that our differences enrich us and help us to find creative solutions and generate innovative ideas. We pride ourselves on creating an inclusive work environment where all employees can reach their full potential.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/quantum-systems-gmbh/senior-rust-developer-london-483441","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792312288},{"slug":"graduate-cybersecurity-threat-researcher-position-located-in-cheltenham-united-kingdom-93373","company_name":"knowbe4","title":"Graduate Cybersecurity Threat Researcher (Position located in Cheltenham, United Kingdom)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KnowBe4 empowers the modern workforce to make smarter security decisions every day. Trusted by more than 70,000 organizations worldwide, KnowBe4 is the pioneer of digital workforce security, securing both AI agents