&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe that creating an environment where everyone feels a sense of belonging is central to our culture and that diversity is paramount to driving creativity, innovation, and value for our clients and for our people.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;An award-winning workplace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;You can be a part of our ‘Great Place to Work’ – with our commitment to women and well-being in the workplace for all. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/en/impact/awards/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Click here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; to see some of our recent awards and how we’ve achieved this.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Using business as a force for good.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We maintain high standards of environmental performance and transparency, which can be seen through our commitment to Net Zero with our SBTI-verified Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions reduction targets and our support of the Better Business Act. We report our progress publicly and ensure that we are also externally assessed and scored through organisations like CDP and EcoVadis - helping us to continually identify where we can improve.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:200,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We have a long legacy of supporting the communities in which we work, and offer a variety of ways to contribute, by putting people first and creating impact that lasts. Our Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) agenda is about giving back to the communities in which we live and work by sharing our skills, talent and time. In essence, we aim to empower and encourage everyone in the firm to contribute to the things we care about, and support registered charities and organisations with a clear social or environmental purpose to increase the positive impact they can have.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(208, 0, 111); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot; data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Join us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot; data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;All applications received will be reviewed by a member of our Talent Acquisition team. We never rely solely on automated screening or AI tools to make hiring decisions. Your application will be considered for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, nationality, disability, age, faith or social background. We do not filter applications by university background and encourage those who have taken alternative educational and career paths to apply. We would like to actively encourage applications from those who identify with less represented and minority groups. We operate an inclusive recruitment process, ensuring reasonable adjustments where needed. Please contact a member of our Recruitment Team to discuss further.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(208, 0, 111); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot; data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Baringa Privacy Notices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For UK &amp;amp; EU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-004-ukrpn---uk-recruitment-privacy-notice-pdf.pdf&quot;&gt;UK Recruitment Privacy Notice / &lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-005-eurpn---eu-recruitment-privacy-notice-pdf.pdf&quot;&gt;EU Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;, to evaluate your application and meet our legal and reporting obligations. In line with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right to request access to, rectification, or erasure (subject to legal limitations) of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For the USA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your personal data may be retained by Baringa for up to two years, as outlined in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp;amp; APAC)&lt;/a&gt;, to support the recruitment process and internal reporting requirements. Where applicable, and in accordance with relevant federal and state laws, you may have the right to request access to or correction of your personal information. For further details, please contact &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Australia &amp;amp; Singapore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp;amp; APAC)&lt;/a&gt;, to assess your application and meet applicable reporting and legal obligations. In line with the Australian Privacy Act and Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), you may have rights to access, correct, or request limited deletion of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at &lt;a ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/baringa/consultant-or-senior-consultant-consumer-products-retail-london-369808","tags":["Consumer Products and Retail"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792302919},{"slug":"senior-sales-manager-issuing-london-325873","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Senior Sales Manager - Issuing","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Checkout.com are actively looking for an enthusiastic and talented Senior Sales Manager to join our Commercial Team in London to drive rapid growth  for our revolutionary Card Issuing solution. We need a high-achieving individual to help global enterprises launch modern card programs—from virtual cards for travel intermediaries to physical cards for BNPL.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are a driven and focused salesperson with a proven track record of selling cutting edge issuing solutions in a high-growth and competitive environment, this is the role for you. In return, on top of a tremendous working environment, we offer you an unrivalled uncapped recurring commissions plan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the Director, the Senior Sales Manager will handle multiple sales cycles, always ensuring a high conversion rate and outperforming the sales targets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Along the way, you'll collaborate closely with various in-house talents across Technology and Business to position our capabilities, products, services and solutions effectively with prospects. The ideal candidate will need to be an independent, high-achieving individual, able to stand out in an entrepreneurial environment and outperform sales targets through personal drive.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>How You’ll Make an Impact</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pipeline Growth: Identify the most promising clients and grow a healthy pipeline for card issuing across various verticals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solution Selling: Sell our issuing products to travel intermediaries and fintech clients through outbound techniques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consultative Expert: Help prospects evaluate Checkout.com, handling  detailed questions about our product capabilities, serving as a consultant and industry expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proposal Management: Prepare thorough presentations and proposals that highlight the ROI of switching to a modern issuer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full Cycle Orchestration: Lead the entire Sales process, acting as the main point of contact for clients and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration: Partner with other Sales team members to share best practices, key business insights and industry trends</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Market Intelligence: Provide feedback on local trends including competitor insights, customer needs, sales, product and marketing information</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience: 5+ years of Sales experience, with at least 3 years specifically within Payments or Card Issuing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Network: A solid network of potential prospects and partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI &amp; Productivity: Proficient in leveraging AI-powered sales tools to augment prospecting and analyze deal intelligence to accelerate the sales cycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Passion: Tech-savvy with a passion for how technology is transforming finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business Acumen: Solid understanding of financial factors, including interchange mechanics and card scheme products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Soft Skills: Exceptional communication and negotiation techniques, with the ability to navigate complex, multi-stakeholder deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tools: Knowledge of Salesforce and a highly organized approach to prioritizing shifting workloads.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/senior-sales-manager-issuing-london-325873","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792302022},{"slug":"strategic-customer-success-manager-london-418438","company_name":"incident.io","title":"Strategic Customer Success Manager","description":"<h1>A little about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is the AI software reliability platform trusted by engineering teams at Netflix, Etsy, and 2,000+ companies who can't afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stakes are real, the talent is insane, and somehow it's a genuinely lovely place to work. We all pull our weight, go the extra mile, and put in the bit of magic most companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $100+ million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role in one line</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our first EMEA Strategic Customer Success Manager, you’ll help define what strategic success looks like at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a>, and become the trusted partner who makes us core to how the biggest enterprises run reliability.</p><h2>What that looks like day to day</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work with a small number of our largest, most complex and highest-value customers. These are established, often global and regulated enterprises, where buying decisions take time, many business units are involved, and incident management is part of a wider move away from legacy tools and processes. You’ll be their strategic partner across the full lifecycle, from early involvement in the deal with Sales through to adoption and expansion, and from the on-call engineer to the CIO and CTO.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll help land strategic logos with focused first contracts, then build the business case and success plan that turns them into larger deals. From there you’ll expand across the enterprise, mapping the organisation, finding champions and repeating proven wins across business units and regions. You’ll run Executive Business Reviews and connect our leadership with theirs, tying what we do to what matters to their business: operational resilience, regulatory risk, the cost of downtime, tool consolidation, MTTR reduction and incident process maturity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll lead onboarding and migrations in organisations that move carefully, moving them off legacy tools and ITSM-led processes and making the change stick, including deeper adoption across Response, On-call, Status Pages and our AI capabilities. You’ll spot and reduce business, operational and reputational risk before it becomes visible, and bring Sales, Solutions Engineering, Product, Marketing and Support together around shared goals for each account, including expansion and renewals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll also work directly with Product and Engineering on the roadmap and design partnerships. As the first EMEA Strategic CSM and third on the team overall, you’ll help define our strategic CS playbook, support high-stakes deals and help develop your peers as the segment grows.</p><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have significant experience in Customer Success, Account Management or Technical Account Management, managing strategic or Fortune 500-scale accounts in enterprise SaaS. Traditional enterprises like financial services, insurance, pharma, retail or private equity are ideal. Developer tooling, observability or incident management is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve driven adoption, retention and expansion in large, complex accounts with many stakeholders, and you have results you can point to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know how to land small and grow large, turning a pilot or single business unit into a multi-BU footprint over a long sales cycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building a business case doesn’t faze you, nor does navigating procurement, security, legal and change management in slow-moving organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re confident with senior technical executives, running EBRs and strategic planning sessions, and just as comfortable going deep with SREs and platform engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re technically fluent in modern engineering organisations, on-call, incident response, SRE practices and the observability and DevOps ecosystem, and you can translate it for business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong commercial judgement, partner well with Sales on renewals and expansion, and get ahead of customer challenges rather than reacting to them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re autonomous and comfortable with ambiguity. You’re excited to define the role, not just step into it.</p></li></ul><h2>Supporting you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover - we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful equity.</strong> We’re rapidly scaling, and everyone who helps shape the outcome should share in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited AI spend.</strong> For everyone, not just engineers. We’re all-in on AI across the company, and we expect you to be too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous parental leave.</strong> The early days with a new baby matter more than anything we’re doing here, and we want you to be present for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Two budgets that have your back.</strong> £1000 to invest in your setup, £500 a year to invest in yourself.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/incidentio/strategic-customer-success-manager-london-418438","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792302021},{"slug":"director-of-quality-london-108201","company_name":"Lilt Corporate","title":"Director of Quality","description":"<h1><strong>About LILT</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI is changing how the world communicates — and LILT is leading that transformation.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're on a mission to <strong>make the world's information accessible to everyone</strong>, regardless of the language they speak. We use cutting-edge <strong>AI, machine translation, and human-in-the-loop</strong> expertise to translate content faster, more accurately, and more cost-effectively without compromising on brand, voice, or quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> At LILT, we empower our teammates with leading tools, global collaboration, and growth opportunities to do their best work. Our company virtues—<strong>Work together, win together; Find a way or make one; Dance in the customer's shoes; Quicker than they expect; Quality is Job 1</strong>—guide everything we do. We are trusted by<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/intel-corporation/"> Intel Corporation</a>,<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/canva/"> Canva</a>, the<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/deptofdefense/"> United States Department of Defense</a>, the<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/united-states-air-force/"> United States Air Force</a>,<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/asics/"> ASICS</a>, and hundreds of global Enterprises. Backed by Sequoia, Intel Capital, and Redpoint, we’re building a category-defining company in a $50B+ global translation market being redefined by AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote or hybrid, EMEA or US Eastern time zone</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team:</strong> Production, Quality</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reports to:</strong> VP Production</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct reports:</strong> Quality Manager (AMER, customer staffing) and 2 Quality Coordinators</p><h3>About the role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Director of Quality, you will own LILT's quality system end to end: standards, audit, compliance, procedures, continuous improvement, and the roadmap and operation of our <strong>Quality Agents</strong>. You'll help move Quality from a primarily reactive, execution-led function to a proactive, data-driven partner for customers and internal teams, with quality designed into our AI-native workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be the person who can run a customer audit while simultaneously shipping an improved agent evaluation. As the single Quality partner for Customer Success, Production, Research and Product, you'll turn customer requirements into measurable acceptance criteria, effective controls and better models and workflows. You'll advise customers on the right quality, cost and speed mix, including where automated, agent-verified and human-verified workflows are appropriate, with stronger assurance for high-risk and regulated content.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a hands-on Quality SME and operator with real depth in both worlds: experience designing and building AI agents and improving LLM output, and a solid grounding in traditional quality management. You'll bring senior expertise in data, AI, customer advisory and process, and make sure quality work prevents recurrence rather than stopping at rework or ticket closure.</p><h3>What you'll do</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality Agent leadership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate, design and build reliable Quality Agents with well-defined tools and clear, structured instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use orchestration patterns to evolve from a single agent to multi-agent systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define evaluation criteria, test sets and success metrics for agent performance, and run agents in production with clear monitoring and escalation paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive adoption across teams and show measurable reductions in manual quality effort.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Research and Product partnership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Research and Product on ADQ, LLM model improvements, AI Review, AI QA, and new and emerging AI workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn quality findings into product requirements, evaluation criteria and continuous feedback loops that improve model and workflow output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the voice of quality in roadmap discussions, and help decide where human review, AI review or both are needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Audit, compliance and procedure</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own LILT's approach to internal and external audits, including ISO certification (e.g. ISO 17100, ISO 18587, ISO 9001) and customer audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and run periodic internal audits, manage evidence collection, and track corrective and preventive actions to closure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standardise and maintain SOPs, workflows and quality documentation, and keep them current as AI workflows change how we work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure quality processes meet customer, contractual and regulatory requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer advisory</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Customer Success and Delivery to define proactive quality programmes, success metrics and governance for strategic accounts, including AI-forward enterprise and life science / regulatory programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate customer quality requirements into clear pre-delivery acceptance criteria, validation methods and risk-appropriate controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customers on the right quality, cost and speed mix and where automated, agent-verified, human-verified or combined workflows are appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent LILT's quality function as a credible subject-matter authority in customer business reviews, audits and escalations, using quality data and metrics to demonstrate fitness for purpose.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuous improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead structured CI across the Commercial business: root cause analysis, corrective and preventive actions, KPI reviews and retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own a proactive quality metrics framework that makes errors, PQs, rework and trends visible, and use it to prioritise improvements and demonstrate outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen quality controls across review, delivery and follow-through, including mandatory account-specific checks, intervention on critical findings and clear escalation ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product and Engineering to automate checks and escalation, and verify that corrective actions prevent recurrence rather than ending at rework or ticket closure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expert Operations partnership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Expert Supply and Ops to embed processes, guidance and quality feedback that maintain a high-quality pipeline of experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use quality findings and recurring failure patterns to improve expert qualification, guidance and ongoing quality management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team leadership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and develop the Quality team, including the customer-facing Quality Manager and Quality Coordinators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish the team's operating cadence and evolve how the team works as Quality Agents reduce manual coordination work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee embedded Quality Manager staffing sold as a service to customers, ensuring the role owns the specific quality programmes and initiatives those customers pay for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop playbooks for AI-driven quality management and keep staffing-as-a-service delivery aligned with LILT's quality standards.</p></li></ul><h3>What you'll bring</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agent design and build:</strong> demonstrable, hands-on experience designing, building and running LLM-based agents in production. Please be ready to walk us through agents you have built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven quality management:</strong> scripting or data skills (e.g. Python, SQL), with experience turning quality data into actionable metrics, preventive controls and measurable improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>LLM model improvement:</strong> proven experience improving LLM output quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Significant experience running quality systems</strong>, including leading audits (internal and external), compliance programmes, and writing and maintaining processes and procedures. Quality certifications such as Six Sigma are a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading <strong>structured CI</strong> (RCA, CAPA, KPI reviews).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing and developing people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer advisory and cross-functional partnership:</strong> a clear communicator who can translate customer quality requirements into acceptance criteria and governance, advise on quality, cost and speed trade-offs, and work credibly with customers, executives and technical teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in localisation, translation or language services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in customer-facing quality roles for enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Research and Product collaboration:</strong> a track record of working with research scientists and product managers to turn quality insight into product requirements and shipped improvements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our Story</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our founders, Spence and John met at Google working on Google Translate.  As researchers at Stanford and Berkeley, they both worked on language technology to make information accessible to everyone. While together at Google, they were amazed to learn that Google Translate wasn’t used for enterprise products and services inside the company.The quality just wasn’t there. So they set out to build something better. LILT was born.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">LILT has been a machine learning company since its founding in 2015. At the time, machine translation didn’t meet the quality standard for enterprise translations, so LILT assembled a cutting-edge research team tasked with closing that gap. While meeting customer demand for translation services, LILT has prioritized investments in Large Language Models, human-in-the-loop systems, and now agentic AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With AI innovation accelerating and enterprise demand growing, the next phase of LILT’s journey is just beginning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our Tech</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">What sets our platform apart:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brand-aware AI that learns your voice, tone, and terminology to ensure every translation is accurate and consistent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agentic AI workflows that automate the entire translation process from content ingestion to quality review to publishing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">100+ native integrations with systems like Adobe Experience Manager, Webflow, Salesforce, GitHub, and Google Drive to simplify content translation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Human-in-the-loop reviews via our global network of professional linguists, for high-impact content that requires expert review</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>LILT in the News</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Featured in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.thesoftwarereport.com/the-top-100-software-companies-of-2024/"><u>The Software Report’s</u></a> Top 100 Software Companies!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">LILT makes it onto the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://labs.lilt.com/lilt-listed-on-the-2024-inc-5000"><u>Inc. 5000 List</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">LILT’s continues to be an intellectual powerhouse, holding <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://patents.justia.com/inventor/john-sturdy-denero"><u>numerous patents</u></a> that help power the most efficient and sophisticated AI and language models in the industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lilt.com/news"><u>all our news on our website</u></a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><