hlight-dark dark:active:s-text-highlight-dark-night" ---------- schreiben. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.pennylane.com/fr/vos-donnees-personnelles-recrutement">Mehr erfahren</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🇪🇸 <strong>Datos personales</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pennylane trata sus datos para gestionar su candidatura y evaluar su idoneidad para el puesto. En caso de que su candidatura no sea seleccionada, sus datos podrán conservarse hasta 2 años a partir de nuestro último contacto o de la finalización del proceso de selección, con el fin de constituir y gestionar una reserva de candidatos. Puede oponerse en cualquier momento y solicitar la eliminación de sus datos escribiendo a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" ---------- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.pennylane.com/fr/vos-donnees-personnelles-recrutement"><strong>Más información</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/pennylane-sas/ciso-paris-281818","tags":["Financial Services"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"All France (remote)","created_at":1792291216},{"slug":"financial-services-regulatory-lead-h-f-paris-88777","company_name":"Pennylane SAS","title":"Financial Services Regulatory Lead H/F","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you looking to have an impact on the daily life of millions of entrepreneurs in France (and tomorrow in Europe)?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you looking for a work environment that values trust, proactivity, and autonomy?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Then Pennylane is the right place for you !</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our vision</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to become the most beloved financial Operating System of French SMEs and Accounting Firms (and soon, European ones).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We help entrepreneurs rid themselves of time-consuming tasks related to accounting and finance while providing them with access to key financial information to assist in making the best decisions for their business.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pennylane is one of the fastest growing Fintechs in France (and soon to be in Europe!)</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">In 5 years of existence, we’ve managed to :</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Make ourselves known as a groundbreaking accounting and financial software for small businesses and their accountants</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Raise a total of €400 millions, including from Sequoia, the famous fund from the Silicon Valley who invested early in companies like Google, Facebook, Airbnb, Stripe, Paypal and much more...</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 Grow from 7 cofounders to 1000 happy Pennylaners : we’re now recognized as one of the greatest places to work in France (and also remotely), with a 4.6/5 rating on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.fr/Avis/Pennylane-France-Avis-E4171708.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 Build an international environment with more than 25 nationalities, with a strong remote-friendly culture, where 30% of the employees are already working from all parts of Europe</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 Earn the trust of thousands of customers and accounting firms and obtain <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/search?q=pennylane&amp;ei=O9pOYvm0Co-blwSmhKmIAw&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi5vsWL-4H3AhWPzYUKHSZCCjEQ4dUDCA4&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=pennylane&amp;gs_lcp=Cgdnd3Mtd2l6EAMyDQgAEIAEELEDEIMBEAoyCwguEIAEEMcBEK8BMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKMgUIABCABDIFCAAQgAQyBQgAEIAEMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKOgcIABBHELADOgkIABCwAxAKEEM6CgguEMcBEK8BEAo6BggAEBYQHjoICAAQFhAKEB46DQguEIAEEMcBEK8BEApKBAhBGABKBAhGGABQ7QFY6wVgugdoAXABeACAAUiIAbMCkgEBNZgBAKABAcgBCcABAQ&amp;sclient=gws-wiz">outstanding ratings</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Already more than 1 300,000 small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and over 6000 accounting firms use Pennylane in France!</p><h2><br /></h2><h2>Why is this role important for Pennylane?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pennylane is building Pennylane Financial Services (PFS), a newly created regulated subsidiary applying for ACPR authorisations as a payment institution and a financing company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From day one of licensing, PFS must be able to operate in full regulatory compliance - not only through policies, but through reliable execution: clear ownership, predictable reporting routines, auditable evidence, and effective coordination across Operations, Finance/Accounting and Compliance &amp; Risk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is critical to organise and run that regulatory function, with the ambition to progressively consolidate regulatory reporting ownership within PFS.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How will you contribute to the project?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will help build and operate the regulatory office of Pennylane Financial Services, working across Compliance &amp; Risk, Finance, Legal, Operations and Technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your initial priority will be to turn PFS’s regulatory requirements into a reliable operating framework: a complete obligations inventory, clear ownership, an integrated regulatory calendar, and effective controls over regulatory reporting and evidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In practice, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">maintain the authoritative inventory of PFS’s regulatory obligations;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">coordinate the regulatory-reporting portfolio and directly produce selected returns;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">establish clear responsibilities, reporting controls and escalation paths across contributing functions;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">support supervisory responses and commitment tracking from day one;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">coordinate regulatory change with Compliance, Legal and the relevant subject-matter owners; and</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">support regulatory governance through clear reporting, decision tracking and follow-through.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will not replace the specialist accountability of Finance, the MLRO, Legal, Risk or Operations. Your role will be to make their contributions converge into a controlled, timely and inspection-ready regulatory process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As PFS grows, you will help shape and evolve its regulatory operating model and governance arrangements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What will your day-to-day responsibilities be?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain the regulatory-obligations inventory:</strong> keep a complete and current view of PFS’s recurring and event-driven obligations, with clear owners, deadlines, controls, approval routes and evidence requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the integrated regulatory calendar:</strong> coordinate contributors, dependencies and review milestones across Compliance &amp; Risk, Finance, Legal, Operations and Technology, escalating delivery risks before deadlines are affected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordinate regulatory reporting:</strong> oversee the end-to-end reporting portfolio and directly prepare selected returns, while ensuring specialist functions retain accountability for their underlying judgements and data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Establish reporting controls:</strong> document and operate source-to-report lineage, reconciliations, variance analysis, maker-checker review, sign-offs, submission evidence, correction procedures and backup arrangements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordinate data-quality remediation:</strong> document reporting-data issues, assign them to the accountable function, monitor resolution and escalate overdue or recurring problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support supervisory responses and commitment tracking:</strong> maintain a reliable record of requests, responses and commitments; coordinate contributions and evidence under the direction of the ACPR relationship owner; and escalate delivery issues to PFS management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coordinate regulatory change:</strong> work with Compliance, Legal and relevant subject-matter owners to translate new requirements into impact assessments, accountable owners, implementation plans and evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support regulatory governance:</strong> prepare concise status reporting, maintain decision and action tracking, and ensure regulatory matters reach the appropriate management or governance forum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve tools and processes:</strong> define practical requirements for workflow, evidence storage, reporting production and regulatory remittance, reducing manual effort without weakening controls.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Profile we are looking for</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful experience in a regulated financial environment, in one or more areas such as regulatory reporting, regulatory operations, prudential reporting, compliance, risk, finance, internal control or regulatory advisory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of reporting controls and data quality, including reconciliations, source-to-report traceability, review and approval controls, exception management and auditable evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound regulatory judgement: ability to understand a requirement, identify its practical implications, recognise when specialist Legal or Compliance input is needed, and translate conclusions into ownership, processes and controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong execution discipline, with a demonstrated ability to coordinate recurring deliverables, manage interdependencies and meet fixed deadlines reliably.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work effectively across Finance, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Operations and Technology, while preserving clear accountability between functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to build structured and durable ways of working—including registers, calendars, procedures, templates and knowledge bases—in an evolving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear and concise written and verbal communication, including the ability to explain issues, assumptions and required decisions to senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional fluency in French and English.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ACPR reporting, supervisory interactions or the French regulatory environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a payment institution, electronic-money institution, financing company, bank, regulated fintech, supervisory authority or specialist advisory firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to more than one regulatory domain, such as payments, prudential reporting, statistical reporting, AML-CFT, fraud, incidents or financing activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coordinating regulatory change, supervisory requests, inspections or remediation commitments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with regulatory-remittance tools, reporting-data lineage, workflow automation or evidence-management solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or materially improving a regulatory framework in a new entity, licensing programme or operating-model transformation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Recruitment Process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">1. Interview with Simon (30-45 min), Senior Recruiter</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">2. Interview with Laurent (1h), Compliance&amp;Risk Director</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">3. Case Study with two Finance or Legal representative (1h)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">4. Team fit with two interviewers (30 min)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">5. Last round with Maxime and Felix (45 min) </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What do we do to make your work life easier</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 Wherever you are based, you will get 25 vacations days paid by Pennylane</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💵 You’ll have a competitive compensation package</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 You'll get company shares to enjoy a piece of the success story you're building with us</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏡 You’ll have a budget to turn your home into a more comfortable workspace, as well as a monthly allowance to work from a coworking space whenever you feel like it</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⛹️ Through our partner Gymlib, you’ll have access to 8000 fitness spaces in Europe and more than 300 activities related to wellness</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 You’ll get the latest Apple equipment</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏢 Depending on the teams and the requirements of the position - you'll be able to work remotely from your country of residence, as long as it is in Europe and within a maximum time difference of two hours from the CET time zone</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎉 We are committed to regularly coming together for company events such as Tech Days (which bring remote Pennylaners together every 3 months) or our annual company seminar, fostering significant moments of cohesion for everyone.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are based in France, you will have a French contract following French regulation on top of the additional perks : 6 to 12 RTT, 5 weeks PTOs, lunch credits (Swile), Alan Blue healthcare cover and regular events in cities where Pennylaners are mostly presents (Lyon, Bordeaux, Nantes…)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We're working on providing those last advantages to our people based outside of France as well, but it can be quite more complex depending on different countries.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who are we looking for ?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To thrive at Pennylane, you need :</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-To speak English (level is assessed and appreciated according to the department you’re applying to)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-To be energized by an ever-shifting work environment</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-To be highly collaborative (within your team or other stakeholders)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-Sufficiently experienced to prioritize business-led actions on your day to day activity</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that some people are less likely to apply than others, if they don’t feel like they meet the full list of criteria.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re hesitating, we encourage you to apply : who knows, it might be the start of a meaningful and long-lasting collaboration.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Important information for candidates</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment scam attempts are on the rise. We invite you to remain vigilant during your exchanges.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applications through official channels only </strong>: apply exclusively through our job postings published on our official platforms (career site, official partner pages).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Always verify the sender's email address</strong>: our communications are sent from professional email addresses with the domains ----- or ----- style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We will never ask you for payment or financial information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">(bank details, payment for an interview, equipment purchases, etc.) as part of the recruitment process. If such a request is made to you, it is fraudulent. We invite you to <strong>not respond</strong> and to <strong>report it to us immediately</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also want to emphasize that we fully embrace diversity, equity and inclusion and that we’re doing our best to create a safe and inclusive environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to providing an equal employment opportunity regardless of gender, sexual orientation, origin, disabilities, or any other traits that make you who you are. If anything, diversity makes us a more fun place to work at.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🇫🇷 Données personnell