at last, and the belief that great work is still fundamentally human. Our goal isn’t to ship the next feature. Each and every team of Notinos is working to set the standard for how humans work together in the AI era. From building a business’s system of record to making and managing AI agents to automating away the busy work, we care deeply about giving our customers more time for their life’s work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the Role:</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead Notion’s GTM strategy and growth for France, one of EMEA’s largest and highest-priority markets. France is a Tier 1 region in Notion’s country-first EMEA model, with significant room to scale into a standalone, high-growth business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is shifting from a traditional sales model toward a builder-led model with fewer handoffs, stronger technical fluency, and more direct ownership of customer outcomes. As General Manager, France, you will be the second-line leader responsible for overall revenue outcomes, regional GTM strategy, and the operating model for the French business. You will lead through frontline managers, teams of Business Development Representatives, Solutions Consultants and Outcomes Architects as well as partner cross functionally with Professional Services, Channel Partnerships and RevOps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on builder-leader role for an AI-native, country-first GTM model. You will bring Notion’s new GTM model to life in France: moving from a segment-first motion to a country-first, AI-native operating system where teams help customers diagnose problems, design agentic workflows, and build real systems with Notion AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits on the EMEA Leadership Team and reports to the General Manager, EMEA.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be based in Paris. We work from our offices on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays (our Anchor Days) because we do our best thinking and building together in person. We’re looking for someone who’s excited to work alongside the team during those days. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Achieve:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the GTM strategy, operating rhythm, and growth plan for France, with accountability for overall regional revenue outcomes across Sales Assist and Self Serve contribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead as a second-line manager: hire, coach, and develop frontline leaders and IC teams across Business Development, Solutions Consulting, Outcomes Architecture, Forward Deployed Architecture/Engineering, and supporting GTM functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale a country-first GTM motion that brings Notion closer to French customers through local executive engagement, market nuance, and faster field-level decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate the land engine by opening the right front doors, growing professional workspaces, increasing net-new and upgrade opportunities, and connecting self-serve signals to sales-assisted motion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win lighthouse customers and turn them into market momentum by making them wildly successful, telling their story locally, and using those wins to influence peer companies across France.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed Notion’s AI-era GTM model across the team, including agent-enabled customer journeys, first-agent workflow activation, AI/agent demo proficiency, and stronger “build with the customer” motions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make agentic transformation central to the French GTM motion: help customers identify high-value workflows, build and deploy Notion Agents, automate cross-functional work, and measure outcomes from AI adoption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner tightly with Solutions Consultants, Outcomes Architects, Forward Deployed Architects/Engineers, Professional Services, Marketing and Channel to reduce handoffs and deliver faster, more durable customer value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build “sell with” partner motions in France, including partner-sourced pipeline, co-sell plays, enablement, AI/agentic solution packages, and joint account planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish Notion as a visible force in the French ecosystem through executive dinners, field events, startup and community engagement, partner activations, and customer advocacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the voice of French customers back to Product, PMM, Marketing, and EMEA leadership, especially around AI transformation, enterprise requirements, security, compliance, localization, and competitive dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a talent destination in France by hiring builder-oriented leaders and ICs, raising the craft bar, and developing the next generation of AI-native GTM talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive operational excellence across forecasting, pipeline quality, territory planning, inspection cadence, performance management, and cross-functional execution.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who We're Looking For: </h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strategic and hands-on GTM operator who has scaled enterprise SaaS or AI businesses in France and knows how to build a market, not just inherit one. You have led through managers, owned complex revenue outcomes, and created local market momentum through customers, partners, community, and talent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine second-line leadership with builder energy. You can set a crisp country strategy, install the operating system to execute it, and step into the field when needed — whether joining an executive customer conversation, sharpening a pipeline plan, coaching a manager, or helping the team translate a customer problem into an AI-powered, agentic workflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are excited by Notion’s shift to an AI-native, country-first GTM model and believe the best GTM teams will increasingly be builders: BDRs who identify transformation opportunities, Solutions Consultants who build with customers in the room, Outcomes Architects who turn early workflows into durable adoption, and Forward Deployed Architects/Engineers who design the technical systems behind complex agentic workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Skills You'll Need to Bring: </h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12+ years of professional experience, including 5+ years leading SaaS or AI sales &amp; GTM teams in France.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the French enterprise and startup ecosystem, including executive buyer networks, local partner channels, and market-specific buying dynamics across all market segments (commercial, midmarket and enterprise)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven second-line leadership experience, including hiring, coaching, and developing frontline managers and high-performing IC teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of owning and exceeding revenue targets across new business, expansion, and renewal/churn dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agency &amp; Urgency: experience building or scaling a regional/country business in a high-growth or ambiguous environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling, implementing, or leading GTM teams around AI, automation, agentic workflows, collaboration, productivity, developer, or data products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong strategic judgment: ability to define a country plan, segment the market, prioritize accounts and plays, and align cross-functional teams around outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational rigor across forecasting, pipeline generation, inspection, performance management, 