nd Marketingprojekte von der ersten Idee bis zur Umsetzung begleiten? Dann bist du bei uns genau richtig!</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Die cross-ING Group AG ist ein unabhängiges Schweizer Ingenieurunternehmen mit Hauptsitz im Winterthurer Technopark und weiteren Niederlassungen in der Schweiz sowie in Deutschland. Wir bieten unseren Kunden vielseitige Ingenieurdienstleistungen und verbinden technisches Know-how mit innovativen Lösungen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Unser Marketing-Team sorgt dafür, dass unsere Leistungen, Projekte und Menschen sichtbar werden. Dafür suchen wir eine motivierte Persönlichkeit, die uns im Rahmen eines Praktikums (50-100%) während 12 Monaten unterstützt, Neues lernen möchte und Freude daran hat, Ideen in die Tat umzusetzen.</p> <br> <p><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><ul><li><p>Du unterstützt uns bei der Erstellung von Content für unsere Social-Media-Kanäle und unsere Website.</p></li><li><p>Du recherchierst Themen, bereitest Inhalte auf und verfasst Texte für unterschiedliche Kommunikationsmittel.</p></li><li><p>Du hilfst uns bei der Vorbereitung und Umsetzung unserer Fachmessen – insbesondere bei Materialbestellungen, Logistik, Koordination, organisatorischen Aufgaben sowie beim Auf- und Abbau vor Ort.</p></li><li><p>Du kümmerst dich um die Bereitstellung, Verwaltung und Nachbearbeitung unserer Messe- und Marketingmaterialien sowie um Bestellungen und Lagerorganisation.</p></li><li><p>Du hilfst bei der Gestaltung von Präsentationen, Flyern, Newslettern und weiteren Marketingmaterialien.</p></li><li><p>Du unterstützt bei der Bearbeitung von Bildern und Videos sowie bei der Umsetzung kreativer Ideen.</p></li><li><p>Du unterstützt das Team bei administrativen und organisatorischen Marketingaufgaben.</p></li><li><p>Du bringst deine eigenen Ideen ein und lernst, wie vielseitig Marketing in einem Unternehmen sein kann.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Das bringst du mit</strong></p><ul><li><p>Du interessierst dich für Marketing, Kommunikation, Medien oder Design und möchtest praktische Erfahrungen sammeln.</p></li><li><p>Du absolvierst idealerweise eine Ausbildung oder ein Studium in einem passenden Bereich oder hast dieses kürzlich abgeschlossen.</p></li><li><p>Du hast Freude an der praktischen Organisation und Umsetzung von Veranstaltungen und packst bei Bedarf auch vor Ort tatkräftig mit an.</p></li><li><p>Du bist digital affin und interessierst dich für Social Media, Content Creation und aktuelle Trends.</p></li><li><p>Du hast Freude am Schreiben und Gestalten und bringst ein gutes Sprachgefühl mit.</p></li><li><p>Erste Erfahrungen mit Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva oder vergleichbaren Tools sind von Vorteil.</p></li><li><p>Du kommunizierst gut auf Deutsch; Englischkenntnisse sind ein Plus.</p></li><li><p>Du bist motiviert, lernbereit, zuverlässig und arbeitest gerne im Team.</p></li><li><p>Du packst gerne mit an, bist offen für neue Aufgaben und bringst deine Ideen aktiv ein.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Das bieten wir dir</strong></p><ul><li><p>Einen vielseitigen Einblick in die praktische Marketingarbeit.</p></li><li><p>Die Möglichkeit, bei der Vorbereitung und Durchführung unserer Fachmessen aktiv mitzuwirken.</p></li><li><p>Die Möglichkeit, eigene Ideen einzubringen und konkrete Projekte mitzugestalten.</p></li><li><p>Eine persönliche Begleitung und die Gelegenheit, von erfahrenen Marketingverantwortlichen zu lernen.</p></li><li><p>Ein abwechslungsreiches Aufgabengebiet mit kreativen und digitalen Schwerpunkten.</p></li><li><p>Ein offenes Arbeitsumfeld mit kurzen Entscheidungswegen.</p></li><li><p>Einen modernen Arbeitsplatz im Winterthurer Technopark.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Bereit für deinen Einstieg ins Marketing?</strong></p><p>Dann freuen wir uns auf deine Bewerbung! Zeig uns, was dich begeistert und warum du unser Team unterstützen möchtest.</p><p>Bewirb dich unkompliziert über den Bewerbungsbutton – mit deinem LinkedIn-Profil und/oder einem aktuellen Lebenslauf.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/cross-ing-ag/marketing-praktikant-winterthur-202718","tags":["HQ Winterthur"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Winterthur, Zürich, Schweiz","created_at":1792279904},{"slug":"vice-president-product-marketing-excellgene-monthey-366132","company_name":"Archimed","title":"Vice President Product & Marketing Excellgene","description":"<p><em><strong>About ExcellGene</strong></em></p><p><em>ExcellGene is a Swiss biologics development company based in Monthey, innovating in mammalian cell protein expression and bioprocess development. The company develops cell lines (CHO and HEK) and processes that enable biotech and pharmaceutical clients to produce proteins, from early research to clinical use. Its edge is speed and protein expression know-how. ExcellGene also licenses its own proprietary cell hosts, CHOExpress and HEKExpress.</em></p><p><em>ARCHIMED took a majority stake in ExcellGene in late 2025. </em></p><p><strong>The role</strong></p><p>ExcellGene is hiring a <strong>Vice President Product &amp; Marketing</strong> to build its product and marketing function and drive the next phase of growth. This is a new role, reporting into the Chief Executive Officer and part of the Executive Leadership Team, to turn product &amp; strategy into a clear offer and steady demand, working side by side with the Vice President of Global Business Development &amp; Sales and the Chief Scientific &amp; Technology Officer</p><p><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Market &amp; customer insight: </strong>understand customers, market segments, competitors and emerging opportunities.</li><li><strong>Portfolio &amp; product strategy: </strong>shape portfolio around market needs and ExcellGene’s scientific strengths.</li><li><strong>Positioning &amp; value proposition: </strong>clearly articulate why customers should choose ExcellGene.</li><li><strong>Go-to-market: </strong>define and drive GTM strategies for core business and new growth areas.</li><li><strong>Demand creation: </strong>build effective lead-generation programs and targeted campaigns.</li><li><strong>Sales enablement: </strong>equip Sales with insights, messaging and tools to win.</li><li><strong>New growth platforms: </strong>identify and develop new organic opportunities and support the assessment and integration of potential acquisitions.</li><li><strong>Team leadership: </strong>lead and develop the Marketing &amp; Product team (3 people).</li></ul><p>This person will connect market, portfolio, positioning, go-to-market and lead generation. He/she will decide where ExcellGene plays, why it wins, and where the next growth platforms come from.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>Must have</strong></p><ul><li>A scientific background and education, ideally combined with a business or marketing qualification.</li><li>10+ years of relevant experience in product and marketing, including 3-5 years in a leadership role.</li><li>Strong product and marketing experience in biologics. Cell-line development or protein expression is highly valued.</li><li>Experience in a CRO, CDMO or other scientific services business, selling development services alongside products.</li><li>Product marketing and broader marketing, with go-to-market experience at both strategic and hands-on level.</li><li>The ability to turn complex science into clear customer value and a sharp commercial offer.</li><li>A start-up mindset: think strategically, do the work yourself and bring an entrepreneurial, hands-on approach.</li><li>Strong cross-functional skills and the ability to work effectively with scientific, commercial and operational teams.</li></ul><p><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul><li>Good understanding of the US market and of Asian markets (India is a plus).</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Location: </strong>Monthey, Switzerland</li><li><strong>Working model: </strong>Hybrid, on site 3 days per week, ideally Tuesday to Thursday</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/archimed/vice-president-product-marketing-excellgene-monthey-366132","tags":["Marketing","Venture Capital & Private Equity","Portco"],"job_types":["Full time","executive"],"location":"Monthey, Switzerland","created_at":1792246825},{"slug":"senior-embedded-performance-engineer-zurich-404854","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Senior Embedded Performance Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;Auterion builds a cutting-edge operating system for autonomous robotic systems that empower a diverse range of platforms to perform surveillance, reconnaissance, inspection, mapping and logistics tasks. Our industry-leading software drives the adoption of robotic fleets and is recognized by the U.S. government as the future standard for its drone programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Embedded Performance Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who is passionate about getting the most out of embedded systems — from low-level Linux tuning and hardware integration to high-performance video and data pipelines. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working close to hardware, moving across the stack, and solving the kinds of problems where milliseconds, bandwidth, startup time, and system efficiency matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the AuterionOS ecosystem on topics such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded Linux performance and system tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-latency video streaming and media pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C/C++, Python, and Bash-based platform development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware integration, system profiling, and end-to-end optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with experienced and driven engineers across Auterion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the Apps &amp;amp; Simulation team and collaborate with other development teams to build high-performance products for autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, optimize, and maintain performance-critical components within AuterionOS, Auterion’s custom embedded Linux distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve end-to-end system behavior across compute, networking, video, and hardware interfaces, with a strong focus on latency, throughput, reliability, and resource efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize demanding workloads such as real-time telemetry, video streaming, media processing, and communication between distributed system components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate system bottlenecks across the full stack, from kernel and OS behavior to application-level code and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to understand both internal and customer use cases, and translate them into robust technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement new platform capabilities with a strong emphasis on measurable performance gains in real-world deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in daily stand-ups, release planning, and prioritization discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc. or M.Sc. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience writing object-oriented C++ and/or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with embedded Linux systems, including cross-compilation, debugging, profiling, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on background in diagnosing and optimizing real-world system behavior, including CPU, memory, I/O, networking, boot time, and application latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or optimizing low-latency video or data-streaming pipelines, ideally on embedded platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of software systems that span embedded devices, higher-level applications, and fully integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals, including system design, implementation, debugging, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with video codecs, GStreamer, RTP/RTSP, or hardware-accelerated media pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Debian/Ubuntu-based systems, Bash scripting, and systemd.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker and docker-compose in complex development and deployment environments, as well as qemu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and performance analysis skills at both system and application level, combined with a proactive and self-directed working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in ROS2/DDS-style middleware and experienced with networking across multiple OSI layers, including REST APIs and performance-sensitive communication paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system integration and interfacing sensors or peripherals, especially via USB and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile engineering environment with stand-ups, sprint planning, and shared ownership across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with build systems such as CMake, including improving build performance in large-scale software projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
