&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;For recruitment and staffing agencies: PHENOGY works exclusively with selected recruitment partners under formal agreements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We do not accept unsolicited candidate submissions from agencies and assume no liability for claims made by unauthorized recruiters regarding our recruitment processes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/phenogyag/sales-engineer-technical-sales-manager-root-419109","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Root","created_at":1792194925},{"slug":"machine-learning-engineer-applied-ai-zurich-427794","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Machine Learning Engineer, Applied AI","description":"<h2><strong>About</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are over 5 billion users using basic applications today such email, notes, tasks, calendar and they're not AI-native. Our mission is to build proactive applications for anyone in the world, who are not used to complex prompting. We aim to bring intelligence to conversations, errands, organising and workflows, with minimal to no prompting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first application is an agent-first mobile communication app. We believe building applications that users use daily for communication, coordination and collaboration needs will help integrate AI into their lives. The net effect is to eliminate misinformation, achieve low coordination costs, enable high quality tasks and collaboration at scale with minimal or little prompting.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML systems that power our AI-native applications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on classification, retrieval, ranking, personalization and evaluation, taking ownership from model development to production deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is for engineers who enjoy solving practical ML problems, improving model quality and shipping reliable systems used by real users.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Focus</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve ML models for classification, ranking, retrieval and personalization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop efficient classifiers and optimize model accuracy, precision, latency and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve search relevance and context retrieval using embeddings, hybrid search and reranking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build personalization models that learn from user behavior while respecting privacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop evaluation pipelines, labeled datasets and metrics to measure model quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fine-tune and adapt existing models when supported by sufficient data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain ML training, inference and deployment pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug production issues, monitor model performance and ship improvements based on real-world feedback.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Tech Stack</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PyTorch / JAX</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embeddings, vector search and ranking models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production ML systems and inference pipelines</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Ideal Experience</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong foundations in machine learning and modern neural architectures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building and deploying ML models in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in classification, ranking, retrieval, recommendation systems or personalization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of model evaluation, experimentation and performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable writing production-quality code and working with real-world datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to balance model quality, latency, cost and reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership, problem-solving skills</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Outcomes</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ML models in production meet expected accuracy, relevance, latency and reliability targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Classification and ranking improvements deliver measurable gains in model quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluation pipelines identify regressions and support reliable model releases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training, inference and data pipelines are robust, reproducible and maintainable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model improvements are driven by real-world feedback and measurable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates effectively with engineering and product teams to deliver reliable ML-powered features.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>How We Work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best products in the world are built by small, world-class teams. We are a high-talent-density, hands-on team. We make decisions collectively and move quickly, balancing high-quality work with continuous learning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining our team requires the ability to bring structure, exercise judgment and execute independently. Our goal is to put a truly magical product into the hands of our users.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Interview Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If there appears to be a fit, we'll reach out to schedule 3, but no more than 4 interviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applications are evaluated by our technical team members. Interviews will be conducted virtually and/or onsite.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value transparency and efficiency, so expect a prompt decision. If you've demonstrated the exceptional skills and mindset we're looking for, we'll extend an offer to join us.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/bjak/machine-learning-engineer-applied-ai-zurich-427794","tags":["ActAI Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1792194022},{"slug":"research-engineer-zurich-327456","company_name":"Sereact GmbH","title":"Research Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<h1>Research Engineer, Manipulation Data &amp; Teleoperation — Zurich</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role owns the data generation layer of Sereact's VLA stack: teleoperation systems and data collection infrastructure that feed Cortex, built from our Zurich research hub.</p><h2>About Sereact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sereact is a Series B embodied-AI company. Cortex, our VLA model, is deployed in live warehouse robotic cells across the EU and US. Zurich is our newest research hub, focused on the manipulation and control problems that sit underneath Cortex.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a Research Engineer position. It is scoped to the data generation layer of the VLA stack: teleoperation hardware and software, retargeting pipelines that map human demonstrations onto robot hands, and the data collection infrastructure that feeds Cortex. It requires building the systems that produce the data those models train on, and working closely with the training team on what that data needs to look like.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and operate teleoperation systems for dexterous manipulation, including retargeting algorithms that map human hand and arm motion onto robot end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and maintain scalable, UMI-style data collection hardware and software that other engineers at Sereact rely on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark control and retargeting approaches using rigorous, human-factors-informed methodology</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instrument and support the physical robots deployed in the Zurich hub, including day-to-day work on the control stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the model-training team to define what data they need and close the loop on data quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tooling or infrastructure outside your immediate brief when it unblocks the wider team</p></li></ul><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc (or equivalent, in progress) in robotics, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field, with a thesis or capstone project on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building a data collection device or system for robot learning (UMI or a comparable system), not just operating one someone else built</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of retargeting algorithms for mapping human input onto robot hands or end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1 to 2 years of combined research, internship, or industry experience in robotics, mechatronics, or a related engineering discipline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software and systems engineering skills strong enough to build and maintain infrastructure other engineers rely on, not only research-grade prototypes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working as an individual contributor in a small, still-forming team</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A conference submission on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting where the candidate is an author (an MSc thesis submitted to a venue like CoRL counts; supervising a student team whose own work was later published does not)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teaching or TA experience in a robotics course</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some exposure to large-model training, even without an independent training record</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A concrete example of building something outside the formal role brief because the team needed it</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-leading AI experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to large-scale compute clusters and proprietary robotic datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A key role in shaping the future of embodied AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and a relocation package for the Zurich area</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sereact-gmbh/research-engineer-zurich-327456","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792183219},{"slug":"solutions-architect-zurich-303054","company_name":"databricks","title":"Solutions Architect","description":"&lt;p&gt;FEQ128R7&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Solutions Architect, you will lead the technical strategy for your customers — owning architecture discussions, driving platform adoption, and serving as a trusted advisor to customer technical leads and architects. You combine deep technical expertise with strategic thinking to position Databricks as the foundation of your customers’ data and AI strategy. You are developing a technical specialization (archetype) and are recognized within your team for depth in a specific domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end technical strategy for your accounts, from initial discovery through production deployment and consumption growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex architecture discussions — designing scalable, production-grade solutions spanning data engineering, ML/AI, and real-time analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor to customer architects, engineering leads, and Directors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical wins in competitive scenarios by demonstrating Databricks’ differentiation through custom-built solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and declare an emerging technical specialization (archetype) — becoming a go-to resource for your team in that domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate cross-functional resources (DSAs, SSAs, Partners) to deliver comprehensive solutions for complex customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence product direction by providing structured feedback on customer requirements and competitive gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
