u Will Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CAD Design &amp; Drafting:</strong> Create clean, fully constrained CAD models, multi-part assembly layouts, and detailed engineering drawings following formal geometric dimensioning and tolerancing standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Data &amp; Configuration Management:</strong> Manage engineering change requests, update bill of materials data, maintain material libraries, and enforce configuration controls in digital product data systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prototype Assembly &amp; Verification:</strong> Build physical prototypes, test assembly sequences, verify fit and tolerance stack-ups, and establish unit build procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Environmental &amp; Stress Analysis:</strong> Perform structural, thermal, vibration, and mechanical shock simulations to ensure hardware survives harsh operational environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manufacturing &amp; Supplier Integration:</strong> Work closely with suppliers to optimize designs for production methods such as CNC machining, stamping, pressing, forging, casting, and injection molding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Interface Management:</strong> Collaborate with electronics, simulation, testing, and systems engineering teams to define physical interface control documents, packaging requirements, and technical datasheets.</p></li></ul><h3>What We Are Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background:</strong> Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CAD &amp; Drafting Experience:</strong> Strong proficiency in production CAD environments with experience applying formal drafting standards such as ASME or ISO GD&amp;T.</p></l