automation-platformen is een pluspunt.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0"><strong>Dit bieden wij</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW76708763 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Een leerzame stage binnen een internationaal Marketing &amp; Communications-team.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Praktijkervaring met CMS-systemen, marketing automation, campagnebeheer en digitale content.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">De mogelijkheid om samen te werken met collega's uit negen verschillende landen.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Ruimte om jezelf te ontwikkelen op het gebied van marketing, projectmanagement en digitale communicatie.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Begeleiding door ervaren marketing- en communicatiespecialisten.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Een laptop en benodigde software om je werkzaamheden uit te voeren.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Een goede stagevergoeding &nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">Flexibele werktijden en een prettige werkomgeving waarin samenwerking centraal staat.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0"><strong>Over Deerns</strong>&nbsp;<br>Deerns is als onafhankelijk ingenieursbureau gespecialiseerd in advies, ontwerp en uitvoeringsbegeleiding op het vlak van installatietechniek, bouwfysica, energievoorziening en duurzaamheid. Onze expertises dragen bij aan duurzame, intelligente en toekomstbestendige gebouwen die de processen van onze opdrachtgevers optimaal ondersteunen. We zijn verantwoordelijk voor het ontwerp van de installaties en het realiseren van een goed comfort en een prettig klimaat in de meest uiteenlopende gebouwen; van kantoren, tot luchthavens en van ziekenhuizen tot datacenters.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0"><strong>Daarnaast is Deerns benoemd als Great Place to Work!</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0">&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0"><strong>Kennis maken?</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW136263344 BCX8">Wil je meer weten over werken bij Deerns? Neem dan contact op met Maarten Borgmeijer (Corporate Recruiter) via +31 6 11 66 75 44.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW136263344 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW136263344 BCX8">Ben je enthousiast geworden? Reageer met jouw cv via de sollicitatiebutton. Je ontvangt binnen drie werkdagen een reactie. Acquisitie naar aanleiding van vacatures op onze website wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Cv's en/of voorstellen die ongevraagd aan ons worden gemaild worden niet in behandeling genomen.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW76708763 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/deerns-groep-bv/marketing-communicatie-meewerkstagiair-den-haag-490453","tags":["Staff"],"job_types":["Student college","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792323077},{"slug":"product-engineer-zwolle-252511","company_name":"Salland Engineering","title":"Product Engineer","description":"<p><strong>Bij Salland Engineering zoeken we een Product Engineer die een belangrijke rol speelt in het goed functioneren van onze pilot line en in de ondersteuning van het productieteam. In deze functie ben je de verbindende schakel tussen productie, engineering en klant.</strong></p><p>Het team Product Engineering, onderdeel van de Semitest Group, wordt steeds belangrijker binnen Salland Engineering. Binnen deze omgeving ben je verantwoordelijk voor het vrijgeven van testoplossingen voor kwalificatie, karakterisatie en productie test. Daarnaast begeleid je kwalificatieruns in samenwerking met de klant, de planner en onze reliability partner.</p><p>Je werkt continu aan verbeteringen en streeft samen met je team naar efficiëntere processen en tooling. Storingen zie je niet als obstakel, maar als uitdaging. Je schakelt snel, denkt analytisch én praktisch en zorgt ervoor dat we optimaal blijven presteren. Je bent zichtbaar op de werkvloer en hebt veel contact met operators, teamleiders, engineeringcollega’s en de planner.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">Een greep uit je werkzaamheden</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Je begeleidt nieuwe productintroducties (NPI) in productieomgevingen;</p></li><li><p>Je beheert en evalueert kwalificatie- en betrouwbaarheidstesten, zoals HTOL, HAST en Temp Cycle;</p></li><li><p>Je analyseert testdata om prestaties, yield en betrouwbaarheid te beoordelen;</p></li><li><p>Je troubleshoot op device-, hardware- en softwareniveau en voert root cause analyses uit bij testafwijkingen, yield drops en product failures;</p></li><li><p>Je verleent technische ondersteuning aan productie- en testteams bij productissues en analyseert en lost device-, test- en procesafwijkingen op;</p></li><li><p>Je borgt soepele overgangen naar high volume manufacturing (HVM);</p></li><li><p>Je treedt op als technisch aanspreekpunt voor klanten en stemt technische verbeteringen af met leveranciers en externe testpartners;</p></li><li><p>Je coördineert technische projecten gericht op testoptimalisatie, yieldverbetering en productinnovatie en stelt product release reports, karakterisatieverslagen en yieldanalyses op.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">Waar ga je werken</span></span></strong></p><p>Aangenaam, wij zijn Salland Engineering uit Zwolle!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Al meer dan 30 jaar ontwikkelen wij oplossingen en leveren wij diensten voor het testen van chips. Onze technologie vind je terug in alledaagse producten zoals smartphones, tablets en auto's. Samen met zo’n 95 collega’s werken we dagelijks aan innovatieve projecten en bedienen we 's werelds grootste fabrikanten van chips en meetinstrumenten.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">Wat krijg je van ons</span></span></strong></p><p>Een uitdagende baan in een hightech-omgeving. We waarderen het nemen van initiatief en verantwoordelijkheid dragen, maar er is meer! </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Wij bieden:</p><ul><li><p>Een aantrekkelijk salaris (afhankelijk van je opleiding en ervaring) tussen de € 3.410,57 en € 4.872,23 bruto per maand (functieschaal: Engineer Expert A) bij een 40-urige werkweek;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een omgeving waarin ontwikkeling centraal staat. Voor ons is het essentieel om een interessante speler in de markt te blijven. Daarom krijg je als medewerker bij Salland Engineering alle ruimte, mogelijkheden en vrijheid om jezelf te ontwikkelen, zo groeien we samen!</p></li><li><p>Uitstekende secundaire arbeidsvoorwaarden, zoals een 13e maand, 24 vakantiedagen, 5 roostervrije dagen en korting op je aanvullende verzekering;</p></li><li><p>Goede werk-privébalans, wij hanteren flexibele werktijden waardoor je de ruimte hebt om privézaken te regelen vóór of na werktijd, af te spreken met vrienden/familie of juist te gaan sporten; </p></li><li><p>Over sporten gesproken, je krijgt bij ons korting op je sport-/fitnessabonnement;</p></li><li><p>Een collegiaal en informeel bedrijf. We ondernemen graag leuke activiteiten met elkaar en hopen dat jij daar onderdeel van uit wil maken.</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">Wat vragen we van jou</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Je hebt hbo werk- en denkniveau, bij voorkeur in een technische richting, met ervaring in elektronica;</p></li><li><p>Je bent analytisch sterk en weet technische problemen gestructureerd te onderzoeken en op te lossen;</p></li><li><p>Je werkt zelfstandig, neemt verantwoordelijkheid en komt afspraken na;</p></li><li><p>Je schakelt makkelijk in een dynamische omgeving en houdt ook onder wisselende omstandigheden overzicht en structuur;</p></li><li><p>Je bent proactief, communicatief vaardig en weet goed samen te werken met collega’s en externe partijen;</p></li><li><p>Je beheerst zowel de Engelse als de Nederlandse taal goed, in woord en geschrift;</p></li><li><p>Je woont in Nederland en hebt maximaal één uur reistijd naar ons kantoor in Zwolle;</p></li><li><p>Als je geen Nederlands of EU-burger bent, beschik je al over een geldig Nederlands werkvisum.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;"><strong>Ben jij enthousiast geworden na het lezen van deze vacature en wil jij werken bij een innovatief bedrijf waar werkplezier belangrijk is? Heb jij de kennis, vaardigheden en de drive die we zoeken?</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Solliciteer dan direct via de <strong>solliciteerknop</strong>. Liever per e-mail reageren?</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Stuur dan jouw cv en motivatie naar: <strong><span ----- class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/salland-engineering/product-engineer-zwolle-252511","tags":["Production Test Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Zwolle, Overijssel, Netherlands","created_at":1792323077},{"slug":"software-engineer-zwolle-373189","company_name":"Salland Engineering","title":"Software Engineer","description":"<p><strong>Do you want to work in a high tech environment where innovation is not a promise, but daily practice? At Salland Engineering, you work on technology for testing the chips of tomorrow. You will have access to state of the art tooling, modern test facilities and an environment where your own ideas, creativity and initiative are valued.</strong></p><p>Salland Engineering is growing fast. This year, we are doubling our effective workspace, further expanding our testers and investing heavily in new technologies, including innovation in the field of photonics. As part of a global player in the semiconductor test market, we combine international strength with the freedom and short lines of communication of Salland in Zwolle.</p><p>As a Software Engineer, you develop C++ software, software calibration protocols and user interfaces for high tech electrical measuring instruments. These systems are used to test the most advanced chips behind the innovations of the future. This role is specifically focused on software development on the PC side.</p><p>Technical challenges do not put you off. On the contrary, you enjoy solving them and working closely together with your software, hardware and firmware colleagues to create smart and reliable solutions. Do you have a completed Bachelor’s degree in ICT, Software Engineering, Computer Science or Electrical Engineering and already have several years of work experience? Are you familiar with C++ software development and do you feel at home in PC side software development? Then it is good to know that this position is not focused on embedded software development. Does it suit you to show initiative and work together with other technical colleagues on highly innovative projects? Then we are looking for you.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#E05598">What you will be doing in your role</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Designing, implementing and verifying drivers (PC-based) for high-tech instruments in test solutions for ATE (Automatic Test Equipment);</p></li><li><p>Designing, implementing and verifying calibration protocols to ensure the accuracy of the instruments;</p></li><li><p>Writing automated tests for hardware validation and developing user interfaces;</p></li><li><p>Keeping information up to date;</p></li><li><p>You are responsible for your own planning and report to your project leader / scrum master.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#E05598">Were will you work</span></span></strong></p><p>Nice to meet you, we are Salland Engineering from Zwolle!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>For more than 30 years, we have been developing solutions and providing services for testing chips. Our technology can be found in everyday products such as smartphones, tablets and cars. Together with around 95 colleagues, we work on innovative projects every day and serve the world’s largest manufacturers of chips and measuring instruments.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#E05598">What will you get from us</span></span></strong></p><p>A challenging job in a high-tech environment. We value taking initiative and taking responsibility, but there is more!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>We offer:</p><ul><li><p>An attractive salary, depending on your education and experience, between €3,866.22 and €5,523.18 gross per month (job scale: Engineer Expert B) based on a 40-hour workweek;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>An environment where development is central. For us, it is essential to remain an interesting player in the market. That is why, as an employee at Salland Engineering, you are given all the space, opportunities and freedom to develop yourself, so we grow together;</p></li><li><p>Excellent secondary employment conditions, such as a 13th month, 24 vacation days, 5 roster-free days and a discount on your supplementary insurance;</p></li><li><p>A good work-life balance. We apply flexible working hours, giving you the room to arrange personal matters before or after working hours, meet with friends/family or go exercising. </p></li><li><p>Speaking of sports, you also receive a discount on your sports/fitness membership with us;</p></li><li><p>A collegial and informal company. We enjoy doing fun activities together and hope that you would like to be part of that.</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#E05598">What do we ask of you</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>A completed Bachelor’s degree in ICT, Software Engineering, Computer Science or Electrical Engineering;</p></li><li><p>At least 5 years of experience in programming C++ applications;</p></li><li><p>Affinity with hardware electronics and the ability to read and interpret electrical schematics;</p></li><li><p>Experience in working with oscilloscopes and other measuring equipment for testing and validating software functionality is a plus;</p></li><li><p>You have a good command of both Dutch and English;</p></li><li><p>You live in the Netherlands and within a maximum travel time of one hour from our office in Zwolle;</p></li><li><p>If you are not a Dutch or EU citizen, you already have a valid Dutch work visa.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;"><strong>Have you become enthusiastic after reading this vacancy and would you like to work for an innovative company where job satisfaction is important? Do you have the knowledge, skills and drive we are looking for?</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Then apply directly via the <strong>apply button</strong>. Prefer to respond by email?<br>Then send your CV and motivation to: <strong><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Acquisition in response to this vacancy is not appreciated.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/salland-engineering/software-engineer-zwolle-373189","tags":["Instruments"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Zwolle, Overijssel, Netherlands","created_at":1792323077},{"slug":"application-engineer-semiconductor-test-solutions-zwolle-34945","company_name":"Salland Engineering","title":"Application Engineer | Semiconductor Test Solutions","description":"<p><strong>Do you want to work in a high tech environment where innovation is not a promise, but daily practice? At Salland Engineering, you work on technology for testing the chips of tomorrow. You will have access to state of the art tooling, modern test facilities and an environment where your own ideas, creativity and initiative are valued.</strong></p><p>Salland Engineering is growing fast. This year, we are doubling our effective workspace, further expanding our testers and investing heavily in new technologies, including innovation in the field of photonics. As part of a global player in the semiconductor test market, we combine international strength with the freedom and short lines of communication of Salland in Zwolle.</p><p>As an Application Engineer, you play an important role in developing turnkey test solutions for testing chips on ATE, or Automated Test Equipment. Together with the customer, you define the test strategy and translate chip and customer requirements into a smart, reliable and best fit test solution.</p><p>In this role, you work closely with chip designers and product engineers from the world’s largest electronics manufacturers. From the first concept to validation and release to production, you make a direct contribution to test solutions that truly make a difference. Within Salland, you work closely with colleagues in the department and with the PCB design team. You are part of an engineering team where sharing knowledge, making smart choices together and building quality are central. Most of your work will be based at our headquarters in Zwolle, with occasional assignments at customer sites.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">What you will be doing in your role</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Set up and validate test strategies and methodologies and document this in an Electrical Test Specification (ETS);</p></li><li><p>Together with a PCB engineer, create hardware schematics for the interface between the ATE and the chip;</p></li><li><p>Develop turnkey, chip-specific test solutions to run on the ATE for testing ICs in production;</p></li><li><p>When requested, characterize the chip according to specifications and report the results;</p></li><li><p>Validate the whole test solution and report the results (GR&amp;R);</p></li><li><p>Maintain close contact with the customer to discuss interim and final results;</p></li><li><p>Responsible for planning and report project progress to the Project Manager;</p></li><li><p>Support colleagues within the engineering team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">Where will you work</span></span></strong></p><p>Nice to meet you, we are Salland Engineering from Zwolle. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>For more than 30 years, we have been developing solutions and services for testing chips. Our technology can be found in everyday products such as smartphones, tablets and cars. Together with around 95 colleagues, we work on innovative projects every day and serve the world’s largest manufacturers of chips and measuring instruments.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#e05598">What will you get from us</span></span></strong></p><p>A challenging job in a high-tech environment. We value taking initiative and taking responsibility, but there is more.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>We offer:</p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">An attractive salary, depending on your education and experience, between € 3.410,57 and € 4.872,23 gross per month (job scale: Engineer Expert A) based on a 40-hour</span><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"> </span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72">workweek.</span></p></li><li><p>An environment where development is central. For us, it is essential to remain an interesting player in the market. That is why, as an employee at Salland Engineering, you are given all the space, opportunities and freedom to develop yourself, so that we can continue to grow together.</p></li><li><p>Excellent secondary employment conditions, such as a 13th month, 24 vacation days, 5 roster-free days and a discount on your supplementary insurance.</p></li><li><p>A good work-life balance. We apply flexible working hours, giving you the room to arrange personal matters before or after working hours, meet with friends or family, or go exercising. Speaking of sports, you also receive a discount on your sports/fitness membership with us.</p></li><li><p>A collegial and informal company. We enjoy doing fun activities together and hope that you would like to be part of that.</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#E05598">What do we ask of you</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>A Bachelor’s degree (HBO) in (embedded) electronics;</p></li><li><p>Affinity with electronics and software;</p></li><li><p>Quick learner having excellent analytical and problem-solving skills;</p></li><li><p>Solution driven and always aiming for the best result;</p></li><li><p>You can deliver high-quality, cost-effective results within agreed timelines;</p></li><li><p>Master the Dutch and English language;</p></li><li><p>You live in the Netherlands and are within a one-hour travel distance;</p></li><li><p>If you are not a Dutch or EU citizen, you already hold a valid Dutch work visa.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;"><strong>Have you become enthusiastic after reading this vacancy and do you want to work at an innovative company where job satisfaction is important? Do you have the knowledge, skills, and drive we are looking for?</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Apply directly via the <strong>apply button</strong>. Prefer to respond via email?</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">Then send your CV and motivation to: <strong><span ----- class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:center;">Acquisition in response to this vacancy is not appreciated.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/salland-engineering/application-engineer-semiconductor-test-solutions-zwolle-34945","tags":["SemiTest"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Zwolle, Overijssel, Netherlands","created_at":1792323077},{"slug":"backend-developer-net-remote-from-eu-deadline-27-10-26-the-hague-27129","company_name":"AlmavivA de Belgique","title":"Backend Developer .Net - Remote from EU - Deadline 27/10/26","description":"<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Write and support backend code in .Net 8.0+ using some of the most common libraries (Newtonsoft.Json, OpenTelemetry, Swagger, Bogus, AutoBogus, Moq);</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Participate in the .NET implementation of a micro-services solution, being able to write backend code in a reliable, fast, scalable, and secure way, satisfying requirements and service level agreements;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Write and support services that read/transform/write data from multiple sources to multiple destinations (APIs, SQL Server, Elasticsearch, Redis, ActiveMq, Graph databases, csv files);</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Review and approve Pull Request created by teammates;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Implement validation mechanisms as unit and integration tests;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Create and manage build and release pipelines and TestPlans in Azure Devops;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Create and manage Kubernetes helm charts for all supported applications and services;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Write and support complex SQL Server Stored Procedures;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Create Kibana dashboards and Elasticsearch queries;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Write OAUTH mechanisms. ADFS knowledge is a plus;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Work comfortably within a team. Follow SCRUM methodology procedures and disciplines; Estimate the work to be done upon request;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Write technical documentation;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Account for secure coding practices, as well as logging and auditing features;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Communicate in a clean, concise way, not only to peers but also to upper layers when needed.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>More than 15 years in IT</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than nine  years of experience in Software Development</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than five years of experience in Back-End Development with .Net Framework in the past seven 7 years</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than three years of experience in designing and developing scalable back-end components (REST APIs, integrations, micro-services)</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than two years of experience with containers and orchestrators (e.g Kubernetes or Docker Swarm)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Experience in more than one  production-ready projects with OAUTH standard</p><p>More than three years of experience in working in an agile/scrum environment</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than two  years of experience with highly scalable systems</p><p class="MsoNormal">More than one year of experience in working in an international/multi-cultural environment</p><p>Good knowledge of application development environments</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of the micro-services design patterns</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of asynchronous programming and messaging patterns</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of .Net Framework 8.0+ (C#)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of Git and the main branch strategies (git flow)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of relational databases (SQL Server)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of message brokers (ActiveMq, RabbitMq or Apache Kafka)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of CI/CD systems such as Microsoft Azure Devops (e.g. Pipelines, Artifacts, TestPlans)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Good knowledge of OOP paradigms and SOLID principles</p><p class="MsoNormal">Ability to draft clear and complete documentation for full stack solutions (including design and architecture)</p><p class="MsoNormal">Knowledge of using Linux shell and basic Linux concepts (e.g., users, groups, rights)</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Deadline 27/10/26</p><p>Only EU Citizens</p><p>Delivery mode: Remote from Europe</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/almaviva-de-belgique/backend-developer-net-remote-from-eu-deadline-27-10-26-the-hague-27129","tags":["Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","freelance"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792323076},{"slug":"senior-adviseur-stedelijke-ontwikkeling-bij-dzp-rotterdam-345728","company_name":"Maximizd","title":"Senior Adviseur Stedelijke Ontwikkeling bij DZP","description":"<p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">🏙️ Ervaring met economische ontwikkeling in steden en regio's? Verdien tot €6.500 + bonus en krijg meer vrijheid in je werk!</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">Bij DZP in Rotterdam krijg je als Senior Adviseur Stedelijke Ontwikkeling de ruimte om zelf richting te geven aan je projecten. Je werkt aan binnensteden, bedrijventerreinen en de ruimtelijke economie van regio's.</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">Je bepaalt grotendeels zelf hoe je werkweek eruitziet, werkt aan verschillende projecten en hebt 21 collega's om mee te sparren.</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">💰 Tot €6.500 bruto per maand + bonus</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">🏠 Hybride werken en veel vrijheid</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">🤝 Een team van 22 collega's</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">📈 Ruimte voor eigen initiatief en ontwikkeling</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">Heb jij hbo- of wo-werk- en denkniveau en ervaring met gebiedsontwikkeling, ruimtelijke economie of vergelijkbare projecten?</p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="cvGsUA block-font-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-start">👉 Zet jouw ervaring in bij DZP en solliciteer binnen 1 minuut!</p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/maximizd/senior-adviseur-stedelijke-ontwikkeling-bij-dzp-rotterdam-345728","tags":["Maximizd | Recruitment Campagne"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1792323076},{"slug":"designer-working-student-employer-branding-amsterdam-143378","company_name":"Teampicnic","title":"Designer Working Student - Employer Branding","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Designer Working Student to help bring Picnic’s people, culture and opportunities to life. You’ll join our Employer Branding team and help shape how candidates experience Picnic, with a particular focus on our LinkedIn page and campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll create and edit visual content for our employer brand, combining design and video to tell stories that catch people’s attention. You’ll also take ownership of the processes behind our LinkedIn campaigns: helping plan content, coordinate assets, publish posts and keep campaigns running smoothly. From a first idea to the final edit and post, you’ll help make sure our content feels distinctive, engaging and true to Picnic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with colleagues across Employer Branding and our wider Creative team of 20+ specialists, including designers, videographers and copywriters. Together, you’ll make content that reaches candidates across the Netherlands, France and Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create employer brand content:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and edit visuals and videos for Picnic’s LinkedIn page, campaigns and other employer branding channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own LinkedIn campaign processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Help plan campaign content, coordinate the assets and timelines, publish posts and keep the process organised from start to finish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring stories to life:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn ideas, interviews and raw footage into clear, engaging content that shows what it’s like to work at Picnic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adapt content for different formats:&lt;/strong&gt; Resize and refine designs and edits for different channels and placements, while keeping the look and message consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support the creative process:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Employer Branding and Creative colleagues to develop ideas, gather feedback and deliver content on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and improve:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep an eye on how content performs and use what you learn to help improve future posts and campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re currently studying Visual Design, Graphic Design, Communication, Media, or a similar creative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited by both visual design and video editing, and keen to work across formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a portfolio or examples of your creative work that show a good eye for detail and a feel for visual storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with, or are keen to develop your skills in, tools such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro and After Effects. Familiarity with Figma is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re organised and comfortable taking ownership of a process, managing details and following through on deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re proactive, open to feedback and happy to roll up your sleeves in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English (Dutch, French or German are a plus!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic perks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀&lt;strong&gt;Every expert was once a beginner!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍&lt;strong&gt;Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪&lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials.&lt;br&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰&lt;strong&gt;Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll receive a gross hourly wage of €16.75, along with a laptop to support your work. Travel costs can also be reimbursed, depending on your location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/teampicnic/designer-working-student-employer-branding-amsterdam-143378","tags":["Students"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792313717},{"slug":"senior-ai-engineer-den-haag-37560","company_name":"Lefebvre Sdu","title":"Senior AI Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Legal AI is only as good as the knowledge behind it. At Lefebvre Sdu, we’ve been building that knowledge for 200 years. Day in, day out. Law by law. Word by word. Other legal AI tools run on our data and software. As the Dutch heart of Lefebvre Group, the European leader in legal and tax knowledge, we’re also developing our own platform: GenIA-L, where lawyers and tax professionals don’t just get <em>an</em> answer, but an answer they’re willing to put their name to. More than 75,000 professionals use it every day, accounting for over €100 million ARR across Europe. We’re looking for a Senior AI Engineer to help shape how the intelligent core of that platform evolves.<br></p><p><strong>HOW YOU'LL MOVE US FORWARD</strong></p><p>GenIA-L is a research platform for legal professionals. A user asks a question. The platform searches our trusted sources and turns them into a usable answer. This is done with agents: specialised AI components that each take on part of the question and work together. In the legal domain, an answer can’t just sound convincing. It has to be correct, and you need to be able to see which source it comes from. This isn’t a pilot: the platform is in production and used heavily every day.<br></p><p>As a senior, you build alongside the team, but you also keep the bigger picture in view. You know the different parts of the platform and how they affect one another. You help prioritise, spot obstacles early and make sure we’re heading in the right direction, both in how we work and technically. You look ahead: where could we go, and what do we need to know to get there? And you help medior colleagues grow by seeing exactly where they’re stuck, without taking the work off their hands.<br></p><ul><li><p>You give direction to the agent architecture of GenIA-L: which specialised agents are needed and how they work together.</p></li><li><p>You break down legal processes and translate them into technical solutions. You decide how the components are best connected.</p></li><li><p>You make sure our knowledge packages and the pipelines behind them can scale and stay up to date. A knowledge package is an expert-reviewed set of commentary, case law, legislative history and practical guidance for each article of law.</p></li><li><p>You build the way we measure quality. Using evaluation sets, observability and metrics, you show that answers, source attribution and reliability are genuinely improving. Not based on gut feeling, but on evidence.</p></li><li><p>You help prioritise the team’s work and flag technical or process risks early.</p></li><li><p>You explore new developments, test ideas in practice and turn them into proposals that make the product sharper or faster.</p></li><li><p>You coach medior engineers and work directly with editors and subject-matter experts.</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></p><p>You have a realistic view of LLMs. You see what they can do, but you also know their weak spots. You follow new AI developments closely, but you don’t just follow the herd: you stay critical and aren’t afraid to say so. You can break a complex problem down into smaller pieces and keep oversight of a system with many moving parts. You take ownership, show initiative when things aren’t yet clear and think from the customer’s problem. You enjoy helping others move forward without taking over. And you like working with lawyers and editors, because they know what a good answer looks like.<br></p><ul><li><p>Extensive experience in software or ML engineering, around 5 years or more. Depth in recent projects counts for more than the number of years.</p></li><li><p>In-depth knowledge of Python and experience with relevant machine learning libraries.</p></li><li><p>You’ve built LLM applications <em>and</em> run them in production.</p></li><li><p>Solid experience with agent frameworks such as LangGraph and LangChain, tool calling, MCP or similar orchestration. Our entire product is built around this. Experience with only a simple search-and-answer setup (RAG) isn’t enough.</p></li><li><p>You’ve made the quality of LLM systems measurable with evaluation sets and observability, and can give concrete examples. Experience with tools like MLflow and LiteLLM is a plus.</p></li><li><p>Strong backend experience, including REST APIs and Postgres databases.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p>Experience in the legal, tax or another knowledge-intensive domain is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>WHAT YOU'RE SIGNING UP FOR</strong></p><p>On Tuesdays and Thursdays, the team works together at the office. What colleagues value most here: mutual trust, room to experiment, and a team that helps each other out when someone gets stuck.</p><ul><li><p>A place where you have influence from day one: on the approach, the processes, and the direction.</p></li><li><p>Colleagues who deliberately chose Lefebvre Sdu over big tech jobs because here, they're building something that doesn't exist yet.</p></li><li><p>Base salary between €5,500 and €6,450 per month, based on a 36-hour week, since that's full-time for us. Plus a lot of extra allowances (see below).</p></li><li><p>A bonus tied to company performance: a fixed year-end bonus of 4% and profit sharing of up to 6%.</p></li><li><p>23 vacation days and a personal choice budget of 12%, of which 8% is holiday pay and 4% is freely allocable. Want more vacation? Just buy it.</p></li><li><p>A bonus of up to 10% of your salary, based on company performance and individual performance.</p></li><li><p>A solid pension plan through PGB, including supplementary partner insurance.</p></li><li><p>Collective insurance plans.</p></li><li><p>A travel allowance of €0.25 per kilometer or a public transport reimbursement, plus an attractive bike plan. For employees with a commute of less than 10 km or more than 60 km, we have an adjusted arrangement.</p></li><li><p>Two days a week in the office in The Hague, within walking distance of Voorburg station. The rest of the week, wherever you work best.</p></li><li><p>Room to grow: in your craft, in your role, in the organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Want to know more?</strong></p><p>We’d love to tell you all about the team and the role. Send us your CV and you’ll hear from us within 5 working days. Any questions first? Message or call Nadine on 06 28556265.<br></p><p><em>A reference check and a VOG (certificate of good behaviour) are part of the selection process.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/lefebvre-sdu/senior-ai-engineer-den-haag-37560","tags":["Product & Technology"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1792312291},{"slug":"ai-engineer-den-haag-337711","company_name":"Lefebvre Sdu","title":"AI Engineer","description":"<p>Legal AI is only as good as the knowledge behind it. At Lefebvre Sdu, we’ve been building that knowledge for 200 years. Day in, day out. Law by law. Word by word. Other legal AI tools run on our data and software. As the Dutch heart of Lefebvre Group, the European leader in legal and tax knowledge, we’re also developing our own platform: GenIA-L, where lawyers and tax professionals don’t just get <em>an</em> answer, but an answer they’re willing to put their name to. More than 75,000 professionals use it every day, accounting for over €100 million ARR across Europe. We’re looking for a Medior AI Engineer to help shape how the intelligent core of that platform evolves.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>HOW YOU'LL MOVE US FORWARD</strong></p><p>GenIA-L is a research platform for legal professionals. A user asks a question. The platform searches our trusted sources and turns them into a useful answer. It does this with agents: specialised AI components that each handle part of the question and work together. In the legal domain, an answer can't just sound fluent. It has to be correct, and you must be able to see which source it comes from. This is not a pilot project: the platform runs in production and is used heavily every day.</p><p>As a medior, your focus is on building. You work independently, on challenges that come from customers and on challenges we spot ourselves. You break down a legal process, translate it into a technical process and work out how to best connect the pieces. Stuck on something? You say so, and your colleagues think along with you.</p><p>You build and improve the agents of GenIA-L and the way they work together.</p><p>You build and maintain our knowledge packages: for each legal article, an expert-validated set of commentary, case law, parliamentary history and practical interpretation. You also work on the pipelines that create these packages and keep them up to date.</p><p>You make quality measurable. With evaluation sets, observability and metrics, you show that answers, source attribution and reliability really improve. Not by gut feeling, but with evidence.</p><p>You build features for customers, such as analysing their own documents and new ways to search case law.</p><p>You work directly with editors and subject-matter experts, and check with them which parts of a legal question really matter.</p><p>You come up with and test ideas to make the product sharper or faster, and alternate AI experiments with back-end development.</p> <br> <p><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></p><p>You have a realistic view of LLMs. You see what they can do, but you also know their weak spots. You enjoy following new AI developments, but you don't just follow the herd: you stay critical. You think in a structured way and can break a complex problem into smaller pieces. You work independently, take initiative when things are unclear and are eager to learn fast. And you enjoy working with lawyers and editors, because they know what a good answer looks like.</p><ul><li><p>You have several years of experience in software or ML engineering. Depth in recent projects counts for more than years.</p></li><li><p>You have good knowledge of Python and experience with relevant machine learning libraries.</p></li><li><p>You have helped build an LLM application that runs in production. Not just prototypes, notebooks or courses.</p></li><li><p>You have hands-on experience with agent frameworks such as LangGraph and LangChain, tool calling, MCP or comparable orchestration. Our entire product is built around this. Experience with only a simple search-and-answer (RAG) setup is not enough.</p></li><li><p>You have measured the quality of an LLM system with evaluation sets or observability, and can give a concrete example. Experience with tools like MLflow and LiteLLM is a plus.</p></li><li><p>You have back-end experience, including building REST APIs.</p></li><li><p>You have experience in Kubernetes. Experience with Postgres is useful.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience in a legal, tax or other knowledge-intensive domain is a plus.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>WHAT YOU'RE SIGNING UP FOR</strong></p><p>On Tuesdays and Thursdays, the team works together at the office. What colleagues value most here: mutual trust, room to experiment, and a team that helps each other out when someone gets stuck.</p><ul><li><p>A good base salary and a standard working week of 36 hours.</p></li><li><p>An end-of-year bonus of 4% of your gross annual salary and variable profit sharing of up to 6% of your gross annual salary.</p></li><li><p>23 holidays and a personal choice budget of 12%, of which 8% is holiday allowance and 4% you can spend freely, for example on extra days off.</p></li><li><p>A good pension scheme through PGB, including additional partner insurance.</p></li><li><p>A travel allowance of €0.25 per kilometre or a public transport allowance, plus an attractive bike scheme. For employees who live less than 10 km or more than 60 km away, we have a tailored arrangement.</p></li><li><p>Hybrid working: two days a week at the office in The Hague, on Tuesdays and Thursdays.</p></li><li><p>Room to grow. In your field, in your role, in the organisation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>WANT TO KNOW MORE?</strong></p><p>We'd love to tell you everything about the team and the role. Send us your CV and you'll hear from us within 2 working days. Any questions first? Text or call Nadine at 0628556265.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>A reference check and a VOG (certificate of good behaviour) are part of the selection process.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/lefebvre-sdu/ai-engineer-den-haag-337711","tags":["Product & Technology"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1792312291},{"slug":"mechanical-test-engineer-noordwijk-54075","company_name":"ATG Europe","title":"Mechanical Test Engineer","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW110874708 BCX8">We are looking for a Mechanical Test Engineer to support the Test Centre of the European Space Agency (ESA) as part of a Workforce Management Service proposal at their location in Noordwijk, The Netherlands.&nbsp;</p><p 