<strong>Tellent Intelligence</strong> team alongside our existing QE team. You'll help shape how we test applications powered by large language models (LLMs) and AI agents, ensuring they are reliable, safe, and deliver high-quality experiences for our customers.</p><p>You'll expand our end-to-end test coverage in Playwright and help build robust approaches for validating AI-powered systems, where quality extends beyond functional correctness. This is a hands-on, collaborative role with genuine ownership, direct impact on product development, and the opportunity to shape how we test AI at Tellent.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>Your 12-Month Journey</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>During your first 3 months:</strong> You'll get to know our <strong>Tellent Intelligence</strong> domain, engineering practices, AI-powered features, and quality standards. You'll learn our testing framework and development workflow while contributing to automated, exploratory, and AI-focused testing.</p></li><li><p><strong>Within 6 months:</strong> You'll take ownership of quality across key AI-powered features, expand our Playwright test coverage, and work closely with engineers to validate AI behaviour, prompts, and model-driven functionality throughout development.</p></li><li><p><strong>After 1 year:</strong> You'll be a trusted quality partner within the <strong>Tellent Intelligence</strong> team, driving improvements to our AI testing strategy, strengthening our automation framework, and helping shape how we build reliable, safe, and responsible AI experiences across Tellent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Work closely with fellow Quality Engineers to bring our test automation strategy to life across the <strong>Tellent Intelligence</strong> domain, taking shared ownership and continuously improving it as our platform evolves.</p></li><li><p>Partner with developers, AI engineers, and fellow QEs to embed quality early in the development process, sharing knowledge and shaping testing practices collaboratively.</p></li><li><p>Design and execute comprehensive test plans, test cases, and automated test suites across frontend, backend, and AI-powered functionality.</p></li><li><p>Develop into a product domain expert, using your understanding to identify risks early and guide quality decisions across the <strong>Tellent Intelligence</strong> domain.</p></li><li><p>Design and execute testing strategies for AI-powered features, validating not only functional correctness but also the quality, relevance, consistency, and safety of AI-generated outputs.</p></li><li><p>Develop approaches for testing non-deterministic systems by creating evaluation datasets, defining quality benchmarks, and identifying hallucinations, bias, regressions, and prompt-related issues as models and prompts evolve.</p></li><li><p>Partner with engineers to validate prompt changes, AI agent behaviour, and safety guardrails, ensuring our AI behaves reliably and responsibly before reaching customers.</p></li><li><p>Continuously improve how we evaluate AI quality by helping establish best practices, quality metrics, and testing frameworks for LLM-powered applications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What You Bring</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Strong QA experience:</strong> Several years of hands-on quality engineering, with senior-level ownership of testing for complex web applications.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI quality mindset:</strong> Experience testing AI-powered applications, LLM-based products, conversational AI, or machine learning systems is a strong plus. If you haven't worked directly with AI before, you're excited to learn and apply quality engineering principles to this rapidly evolving space.</p></li><li><p><strong>E2E automation:</strong> Experience building and maintaining end-to-end test suites in Playwright.</p></li><li><p><strong>API &amp; backend testing skills:</strong> Experience testing APIs and backend services.</p></li><li><p><strong>Balance of product and technical thinking:</strong> Equally at home discussing product behaviour and digging into technical detail.</p></li><li><p><strong>Understanding of AI testing challenges:</strong> Familiarity with concepts such as prompt engineering, AI agents, hallucinations, model bias, evaluation datasets, and AI safety principles is a plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>Analytical mindset:</strong> Comfortable defining quality expectations for systems where outputs may vary while still delivering a great user experience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Communication:</strong> Fluent English for daily collaboration. Polish is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What We Offer</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Hybrid or remote working setup across Amsterdam, the Cologne area, or Poland</p></li><li><p>A chance to shape one of the most ambitious scale-ups in Europe and lead a company-defining tech transition.</p></li><li><p>Work in a diverse, multicultural, and remote-friendly team.</p></li><li><p>€1,500 annual training budget + 2 dedicated learning days</p></li><li><p>Pension plan, travel reimbursement, and wellness perks.</p></li><li><p>28 paid holiday days + 2 additional days to relax.</p></li><li><p>Work from anywhere for 4 weeks/year.</p></li><li><p>Apple MacBook and top-tier tooling.</p></li><li><p>€200 home office budget.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Please note: Benefits may differ based on your employment location.</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>About Tellent</strong></h4><p>Tellent is a leading Talent Management Suite designed to empower HR &amp; People teams across the entire employee journey. Our all-in-one platform combines an Applicant Tracking System (<strong>Tellent Recruitee</strong>), an intuitive HRIS (<strong>Tellent HR</strong>), and powerful Performance Management software (<strong>Tellent Grow</strong>).</p><p>With 250+ team members globally, 7,000+ customers in 100+ countries, and a growing ecosystem of 500+ partners, we help organizations attract, grow, and retain top talent — and we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>AI in our recruitment process</strong></h4><p>We use our internally developed AI tools to help streamline our recruitment process. However, technology never makes a decision. Every candidate is personally reviewed by our team. Your journey with us is guided by people, supported by tech. Curious about how it works? Read our&nbsp;<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://recruitee.com/ai-statement">AI Statement</a>, check our&nbsp;<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://recruitee.com/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, or chat with us at&nbsp;<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>If you require accommodations or support during the recruitment process, please let us know — we’re happy to help.</em></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tellent/remote-senior-quality-engineer-tellent-intelligence-ai-amsterdam-295070","tags":["1. R&D","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792290737},{"slug":"devops-engineer-iam-ping-am-ds-idm-rotterdam-227024","company_name":"Swisscom","title":"DevOps Engineer IAM (Ping AM/DS/IDM)","description":"<p><strong>DevOps Engineer IAM (Ping AM/DS/IDM)</strong></p><p>You'll shape our IAM for the future with Ping Identity platforms. With deep technical expertise and a sense of architecture, you'll shape Swisscom's security promise to our customers. You'll also contribute hands-on to engineering.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What impact will you have?</strong></p><p>The department is organized according to agile principles in a SAFe value strea