-align:justify;">Lead the development and execution of advanced revenue and distribution strategies.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;">Oversee revenue performance across multiple hotels, ensuring alignment with commercial goals.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;">Drive strategic pricing, segmentation, and inventory optimization initiatives.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;">Drive strategic pricing, segmentation, and inventory optimization initiatives.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;">Guide hotel teams in the execution of revenue management best practices.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="text-align:justify;">Lead forecasting, budgeting, and long‑range planning processes.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-align:justify;">Provide high‑level insights to senior stakeholders to support strategic decision‑making.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">This position offers significant influence, visibility, and opportunities for continued professional growth within a forward‑thinking commercial organization.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;"><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Strategic Leadership</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="text-align:justify;">Develop, implement, and continuously refine revenue strategies to maximize total revenue and profitability across the portfolio.</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-align:justify;">Act as a senior advisor to hotel leadership teams, providing guidance on commercial strategy and market positioning.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Market &amp; Performance Analysis</strong></p><ul><li><p>Monitor and interpret market trends, competitor behavior, and demand patterns to inform strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p>Lead complex data analysis to identify revenue opportunities and mitigate risks.</p></li><li><p>Oversee the creation of detailed performance reports, dashboards, and executive summaries.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Forecasting &amp; Budgeting</strong></p><ul><li><p>Lead the preparation of annual budgets, long‑term forecasts, and monthly outlooks.</p></li><li><p>Ensure accuracy and consistency in forecasting models and methodologies.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Pricing &amp; Inventory Optimization</strong></p><ul><li><p>Oversee daily and long‑term rate and inventory strategies across all distribution channels.</p></li><li><p>Ensure optimal channel mix, pricing integrity, and content accuracy.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Cross‑Functional Collaboration</strong></p><ul><li><p>Partner closely with Sales, Marketing, and Operations to align commercial strategies.</p></li><li><p>Support the development of promotional strategies and distribution initiatives.</p></li><li><p>Maintain strong relationships with key stakeholders, partners, and intermediaries.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Systems &amp; Process Excellence</strong></p><ul><li><p>Ensure optimal use of revenue management systems, tools, and reporting platforms.</p></li><li><p>Drive continuous improvement in revenue management processes and standards.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL BRING:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Extensive experience in hotel revenue management, ideally with <strong>multi‑property or regional responsibility</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Degree in Hospitality Management, Business, Economics, or a related field; advanced revenue management education is a strong advantage.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in English; proficiency in Dutch language is a plus.</p></li><li><p>Exceptional analytical and strategic thinking skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable insights.</p></li><li><p>Strong communication and influencing skills, with experience presenting to senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Deep understanding of revenue management principles, distribution landscape, and market dynamics.</p></li><li><p>High proficiency with revenue management systems, BI tools, and analytical platforms.</p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently, manage complex priorities, and lead initiatives across multiple properties.</p></li><li><p>Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and a proactive, solution‑oriented mindset.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;"><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></p><ul><li><p>A competitive salary</p></li><li><p>Travel cost reimbursement and pension contributions</p></li><li><p>A diverse, multicultural, and dynamic work environment</p></li><li><p>Performance bonus based on yearly KPI’s</p></li><li><p>Company assets (phone and laptop)</p></li><li><p>Discounted stays at Marriott, Accor &amp; IHG hotels worldwide and all Odyssey properties</p></li><li><p>Up to 25 vacation days for a healthy work-life balance in the Netherlands</p></li><li><p>Access to Alleo, our internal platform for well-being and development</p></li><li><p>Ongoing training, leadership development, and career growth opportunities</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/odyssey-hotel-group/senior-revenue-manager-utrecht-385750","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Utrecht, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792290734},{"slug":"working-student-solar-regulation-permitting-contracts-amsterdam-240727","company_name":"Fastned","title":"Working Student, Solar Regulation, Permitting & Contracts","description":"<p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Join a fast-growing, listed company with a purpose and inspire thousands of drivers to transition towards electric mobility! Together with 450+ colleagues across Europe, we have the ambition to build Europe's best fast-charging network. We are active in 9 markets across Europe.&nbsp; We have recently been voted best charging network in the UK, France, and the Netherlands, a testimony to our drive to offer the best charging experience to EV drivers!</span></strong></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">The role</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">Our distinctive charging canopies create an opportunity to integrate solar panels (PV) into station design. However, this comes with a cost and certain operational complexity. We are looking for a working student to identify where solar panels create genuine legal, permitting or commercial value to help us review our strategy around this asset.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">What you will do</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Research national, regional and local rules on solar panels regulations impacting tenders and contacts for our European markets.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Review permitting frameworks to determine whether solar panels create explicit scoring, compliance or approval advantages and quantify those.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Review existing Fastned contracts to identify where solar panels is explicitly mentioned and document the requirements around it (energy generation, maintenance etc).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Make a clear distinction between green energy sourcing and on-premises solar panels requirements.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">If time allows: research the influence that solar panels have on customers choosing to charge at Fastned locations.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key deliverables</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A country/region matrix showing legal requirements or clear advantages for tenders.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A country/region matrix showing proven advantages for permits.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">An inventory of requirements around PVs in our existing contracts.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Bonus: evaluation of the value of PVs for our customers.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Who we are looking for</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A bachelor’s or master’s student in law, preferably energy law, environmental law, administrative law, European law, real-estate law or construction law.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A genuine interest in renewable energy, electric mobility, infrastructure and the energy transition.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong ability to read legislation, official guidance, tender documents and commercial contracts.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Excellent written English and the ability to explain complex legal topics clearly to non-lawyers.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A structured and analytical approach, with strong attention to source quality, citations and uncertainty.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Comfort with Excel or Google Sheets and the organisation of a large document set.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Fluency in another relevant language, such as Dutch, French, German, Spanish or Italian, is an advantage.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with planning, permitting, public procurement, infrastructure or renewable-energy projects is an advantage.</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Join us in building a better future</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">We are on a mission to make a positive impact, but we don't forget to recognise &amp; celebrate our successes, big and small. </span></p><p class="p1"><span style="color:#121317">Our benefits package includes:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Enjoy a free</span><strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;daily vegetarian lunch</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;provided in the office.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Break a sweat and improve your well-being with our&nbsp;</span><strong><span style="color:#121317">weekly fitness classes&nbsp;</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">(kickboxing &amp; bootcamp) led by professional trainers.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mental Wellbeing with nilo health:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;Access to a confidential mental health platform offering 1-on-1 coaching with psychologists, group sessions, and a variety of digital self-care tools.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Physical Wellbeing with Urban Sports Club:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;Enjoy a sponsored membership providing flexible access to a wide network of gyms, fitness classes, and wellness facilities across the Netherlands.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You will be provided with a&nbsp;</span><strong><span style="color:#121317">laptop</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;for work (MacBook / Windows).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You can also look forward to other perks, such as food and drinks available all day at the office and various&nbsp;</span><strong><span style="color:#121317">social gatherings</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">!</span><